    thinking: "**Analyzing Verification Plan**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the verification plan and packaging installation requirements, as per the established guidelines. Specifically, I\'m diving into the \"Journeys\" section, starting with the \"Home Scroll Story Journey\" to ensure the proper rendering of the Hero section on the homepage and the inclusion of specific text elements. My aim is to make sure this meets all the requirements.\n\n\n**Exploring User Interaction Flow**\n\nI\'m now deep in the user interaction flow, specifically the plans and navigation journey. I\'m focusing on the click-through from \"Plans\" in the nav, verifying all six plan details, including the comparison table, and then ensuring smooth navigation back. I\'m also addressing mobile reflow, checking the mobile viewport and hamburger menu function, to confirm static and reduced motion behaviors. I also plan to verify the home story works cleanly after navigation, with no issues.\n\n\n**Reviewing Navigation & Rendering**\n\nI\'m now checking the static and reduced-motion states. My current focus is ensuring the StoryStatic renders correctly with stacked SVG sections when motion is reduced, and that the canvas takes the appropriate percentage of the page with the chapter cards underneath, which I\'m evaluating with the ruled notebook page. I also plan to inspect the compare table\'s horizontal scroll behavior and the sticky first column\'s function.\n\n\n\n**Listing Dependencies**\n\nI\'m currently compiling a list of all required dependencies. This includes `gsap` with `@gsap/react`, `lenis`, and the trio of `three`, `@types/three`, `@react-three/fiber` (v9), and `@react-three/drei` (v10). I\'m noting `@react-three/postprocessing` (v3) and `postprocessing` for potential post-processing effects, along with `roughjs`, `react-router-dom`, `clsx`, and `tailwind-merge`. I\'m also including `@radix-ui/react-accordion` and `@radix-ui/react-dialog` for component primitives, keeping the installation constraint in mind.\n\n\n**Verifying Package Installations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on ensuring that all dependencies install cleanly. I need to confirm the versions `install_applet_package` pulls, especially regarding React 19 compatibility with `three` and `@react-three/fiber`. I want to verify if the installation can be batched for the runtime packages and `@types/three`. Also, I\'m checking `node:test` compatibility against `vitest`, and plan to use `node:test` with `tsx` to avoid peer dependency conflicts. I am also planning to review `tsconfig.json` and `vite.config.ts`.\n\n\n**Updating Configuration Files**\n\nI\'m now focused on syncing the configuration. I\'ve noted the brief\'s requirement to update the `@` alias to point to the `src/` directory instead of the root. I\'m updating `tsconfig.json` and `vite.config.ts` to reflect this change, making sure to resolve `@` to `path.resolve(__dirname, \'src\')`. I\'ll also start running `install_applet_package`, and plan to update `metadata.json` and `index.html`.\n\n\n**Confirming Dependency Parallelization**\n\nI\'m now focusing on parallelizing file writes. I\'ve confirmed I can update `tsconfig.json` and `vite.config.ts` concurrently. I am also reconfirming the dependencies for the app: All of the listed packages must be included. Additionally, I am looking at adding `n8ao` in case it is needed by `@react-three/postprocessing`, since it can be either a peer or optional dependency.\n\n\n"
