  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Available Packages**\n\nI\'m currently thrilled by the potential of these packages. I\'ve noted specific versions, including gsap 3.15.1 with its valuable extras, React-related options, Lenis for smooth scrolling, and react-three-fiber. The package compatibility looks great. I\'m focusing on features such as scroll triggers.\n\n\n**Expanding Package Analysis**\n\nI\'m now diving deeper into specific packages. I\'m noting the precise versions of `three/drei`, `@react-three/postprocessing`, `postprocessing`, `n8ao`, `roughjs`, `react-router-dom`, and `@radix-ui/react-accordion` & `dialog`. I\'ve added a \"check:release\" script to the `package.json` file. I\'m focusing on application structure, ensuring modularity and clean files. I will follow provided briefs and rules. I plan to use CSS variables for color tokens.\n\n\n**Defining Color Tokens & Theming**\n\nI\'m currently working to define and implement color tokens. I\'ve established several specific color values such as `--color-soft`, `--color-blossom-50`, and more. I plan to expose all of these tokens within the Tailwind `@theme` block. I\'m also setting up `--color-background` and `--color-foreground` for preset compatibility. I am creating type utility classes and design elements.\n\n\n**Implementing Content Verification**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the implementation of a single source of truth. I am ensuring all copy from `03-STORYBOARD.md` is correctly managed. I\'ve defined `isTodo(value)` to check for \"TODO\" prefixes, and `listTodos()` which recursively gathers content. I\'m focusing on URL handling, particularly in `links`, and ensuring safe fallback mechanisms when URLs are marked as \"TODO\". I\'ve noted specific examples like the `PlanCard` button and `nav` CTA. I\'m also addressing Socials in the footer, ensuring only real URLs are rendered.\n\n\n**Reviewing Logic & Libraries**\n\nI\'m now focusing on core pure logic and library implementations. I\'ve noted the `cn()` helper in `utils.ts` and the GSAP registration in `gsap.ts`. Specifically, I\'m examining `quality.ts` and its test file, noting the `QualityTier` enum and the `QualitySignals` interface. I\'m focusing on ensuring these utilities function correctly and are well-integrated into the project\'s structure.\n\n\n**Assessing Hardware Capabilities**\n\nI\'m now integrating logic for hardware capability checks. I\'ve focused on `webglAvailable`, `reducedMotion`, and other signals. I\'m implementing a `isSoftwareGlRenderer(rendererString)` function and assessing edge cases. The `pickInitialTier(signals)` function, which evaluates these signals to determine the initial quality tier, is taking shape. I\'m focusing on the condition where SwiftShader is detected, as well as addressing weak renderers.\n\n\n**Refining Tier Logic**\n\nI\'m now refining the tier logic, specifically addressing the interaction of `SketchEffect` and `RoomEnvironment` within a headless Chromium environment without a GPU, using SwiftShader. I\'m prioritizing fast rendering and preventing stalls in `playwright-cli screenshot` captures. I\'m focusing on the `stepDownTier(tier)` function, ensuring it progresses correctly (high -> medium -> low -> low) and never returns \'static\' on its own or steps up.\n\n\n**Mapping Chapter Progress**\n\nI\'m now focusing on chapter progress within the overall timeline. I\'ve defined functions for chapter-specific progress (`chapterProgress()`), start points (`chapterStart()`), and names (`chapterAt()`). The `revealRadiusFor()` function, mapping progress to a world-space reveal radius, is also taking shape. I\'m noting specific parameters and ranges for each chapter, such as the `bloom` chapter. Also, I\'ve noted a deterministic roughjs path generator, meaning I can use `<svg><path d={...} /></svg>` directly from `rough.generator().toPaths(drawable)`! This makes `RoughBox`, `RoughUnderline`, `RoughCircle`, `InkArrow` 100% deterministic, SSR/Node-testable, and cleanly compatible with GSAP `DrawSVGPlugin`.\n\n\n**Integrating Smooth Scroll**\n\nI\'m now integrating the smooth scroll provider. I\'m using `ReactLenis` from `lenis/react` when not in static or reduced-motion mode. I\'ve connected Lenis to `gsap.ticker` for updates and trigger calls on Lenis scroll. I\'m exposing `scrollToProgress` and `scrollToId` via context, ensuring a single Lenis instance persists across route hops. I\'m also ensuring that if the tier is static or reducedMotion is true, rendering children natively. I\'m integrating 3-frame SVG filter defs for living ink for the `<LineBoilFilters/>` component.\n\n\n\n**Developing Visual Components**\n\nI\'m now focused on developing visual components using `rough.generator()` for deterministic SVG paths. I\'ve been working on `RoughHighlight` with `RoughUnderline` and `RoughCircle`, `InkArrow` for curvy arrows, and `WashiTape` for semi-transparent, torn tape. I\'m also developing `PolaroidFrame`, `Stamp` labels, and a set of hand-drawn icons. I\'m ensuring all these components have deterministic rendering and support the `drawIn` feature.\n\n\n**Constructing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now building out UI primitives. I\'m developing `Nodey` and `Sprout` mascots with size and boil props, and `Annotation` with a handwritten note and an `InkArrow`. I\'m also implementing a `StickerButton` with specific ink shadow and hover effects. Finally, I\'m integrating shadcn components, styled as paper notes and a ruled notebook page. I\'m focusing on the `doodle-crew-footer.tsx`, implementing the `nodey` crew kind.\n\n\n**Designing UI Primitives**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI layer. I\'m prioritizing the integration of a `sapling` crew kind, `petal`, and `cube` doodle kinds, along with an optional `logo` ReactNode prop. The `Nav.tsx` top bar is taking shape, including Nodey + `petalnode`, \"How it works\" scroll link, \"Plans\" link, Discord/Status/Client area external links, and the \"Get a server\" CTA. The nav will transition based on scroll position and device context. I\'m also ensuring a mobile hamburger menu opens a notebook Sheet. I\'ve designed the page shell to wrap layout elements, including a dev-only todo badge. I\'ve defined a pure deterministic `buildIsland` function for 3D data and textures.\n\n\n**Analyzing Block Generation**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the block generation process in detail. I\'ve noted the footprint of the island, the block count at different size factors (approximately 4,600 at sizeFactor = 1 and 2,750 at 0.6), and the absence of duplicate positions. The seed block at (0, 0, 0) and roots (stone, deep_stone, glow_ore) are ordered by distance with varying appearAt values. I\'m focusing on the placement and grouping of build blocks (cherry trees, house, path, pond) within a specific progress window. Additionally, neighbor blocks (moss_carpet, flowers, lanterns) are also being considered.\n\n\n**Refining Island Textures**\n\nI\'m now refining the island textures. I\'ve developed deterministic 64x64 RGBA pixel painters in `textures.ts` and `textures.test.ts`, which work in Node tests without DOM. I\'ve created Three.js `DataTexture` and `MeshStandardMaterial` caches using `paintBlockTextureData(type, face)` and `paintNormalMapData(type, face)`. I\'ve implemented the albedo, normal, and emissive maps for all 12 block recipes. I\'m using `NearestFilter`, `LinearMipmapLinearFilter`, and `SRGBColorSpace` appropriately. I\'m finalizing textures such as cherry leaves, grass, dirt, stone, and glow_ore.\n\n\n**Integrating Shader Techniques**\n\nI am now integrating shader techniques. I\'m focusing on the implementation of multiple layers per material using custom vertex shader injection via `onBeforeCompile`, to drive GPU drop-in animations, cutaway clip planes/discard during Roots chapter, and subtle vertex wind sway on leaves. Scrolling will be instantaneous, zero-GC, and require no JavaScript loops, even with 5,000 blocks per frame. I\'m focusing on the `StorySetPieces.tsx` component, specifically the shield dome, water pond & waterfall, petals, dusk, lanterns, and fireflies.\n\n\n**Developing Visual FX**\n\nI\'m now implementing visual effects focused on chapter transitions and scene enhancements. I am building dome gradients that change dynamically, instancing voxel groups for mascots, and animating a smooth camera path. My focus is on the `SketchEffect`, which will utilize depth and normal buffers, and `uRevealRadius` for dynamic rendering control. I\'m also ensuring the implementation of the `uSkyRevealed` variable and the sketch effects are outside the revealed sphere.\n\n\n**Implementing Sketch Effects**\n\nI\'m now implementing the sketch effects, specifically focusing on its rendering style: paper-like base with ink outlines from depth, two-direction pencil cross-hatching, and subtle paper grain, to give it a hand-drawn look. The 3D noise will produce a watercolor bleed edge. The sketch effects, along with the specific post-processing effects based on the hardware tier, are taking shape. I\'m also ensuring the performance of island canvas is efficient.\n\n\n**Constructing Story Components**\n\nI\'m now building out the `StoryStatic.tsx` component as a stacked, 6-section version. I\'ve integrated layered `IslandSketchSvg` for ink-only, watercolor fills, and the final PolaroidFrame. This static version is automatically used under reduced motion, no-WebGL, `?static=1`, or WebGL context loss scenarios. I\'m also preparing supporting components like `PlansHighlight.tsx`, `TrustStrip.tsx`, `FAQ.tsx`, `FinalCTA.tsx`, `PlanCard.tsx` (compact and full variants), `PlanGrid.tsx`, and `CompareTable.tsx` with appropriate styling. Finally, I\'m working on the routes and ensuring that `dev` routes are gated.\n\n\n"
