  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Core Modules**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the core modules. I\'ve started outlining `src/lib/gsap.ts`, ensuring key GSAP plugins and `useGSAP` are registered only once. I\'m also working on `src/lib/roughPaths.ts`, building a deterministic path generator using `rough.generator()` that works in both Node and Browser environments.\n\n\n**Designing Island Generation**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing `src/three/island/islandGenerator.ts`. I need to ensure a deterministic voxel island layout, including a reveal schedule, is implemented. I\'m focusing on the footprint, block count, and coordinate uniqueness. The goal is to generate an island meeting all requirements, including varying the size and block count based on a `sizeFactor`.\n\n\n**Mapping Block Appearances**\n\nI\'m currently creating an island\'s reveal schedule, focusing on how different blocks appear over time. I am figuring out how to precisely coordinate block appearances based on their distance from the seed point at (0, 0, 0), ranging from `0.00` to `0.28`. I\'ve started mapping the appearance of several blocks based on that time range, as well as the initial `grass` and `sapling` blocks.\n\n\n**Refining Appearance Details**\n\nI\'m now detailing the block appearance schedule. I\'ve defined precise timings for each block\'s emergence, from the early glow ore veins strategically placed for visibility to the shield layer with its radial dirt and grass. I\'m focusing on coordinated structure groups like paths, ponds, and cherry blossom trees, assigning each a specific timeline for emergence.\n\n\n**Finalizing Reveal Schedule**\n\nI am now completing the island\'s reveal schedule and finalizing the appearance of structures. I\'ve focused on precisely timing the emergence of structures, including the house and its porch lantern. I am also working on the neighbors of the structure, including details like the moss carpet and path lanterns. I am also making sure named anchors like `ore`, `domeRim`, and `house` are implemented to help determine locations and appearances within the island. I\'m double-checking the texture requirements too.\n\n\n"
