    thinking: "**Initiating Unit Tests**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focused on implementing unit tests for our pure logic modules. I\'m using `node:test` and `node:assert/strict`, per the outlined methodology. The first test file to be tackled is `src/content/content.test.ts`, and I\'m ready to begin writing test cases for it!\n\n\n**Prioritizing Test Coverage**\n\nI\'ve prioritized the remaining test files, and am ready to write the test cases. I\'m focusing on determinism and output validation. I\'ll make sure each test is thorough, covering all functions within each module. I\'ll start with tests for `src/lib/quality.test.ts`. After that I\'ll go to `src/lib/storyStore.test.ts`, and then `src/lib/roughPaths.test.ts`. Then I\'ll work on tests for `src/three/island/islandGenerator.test.ts`. I will need to check the block count in `islandGenerator.ts` at `sizeFactor = 1`.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "I1EAa6DiI4P9nsEPgc3VmAY"
