  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Discovering Vite\'s Behavior**\n\nI\'ve made a discovery about Vite. It appears that during production builds, Vite statically replaces `import.meta.env.DEV` with `false`. This is crucial for tree-shaking components like `DevTodoBadge`, `DevSketchLazy`, and `DevTexturesLazy`.\n\n\n**Verifying Vite\'s Optimization**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that Vite statically optimizes `import.meta.env?.DEV`. It replaces the expression with `false?.DEV`, which evaluates to `undefined` in production or testing environments. This approach is superior to aliasing `import.meta` or using the boolean wrapper, as it allows for proper tree-shaking of components like `DevTodoBadge` and avoids runtime errors in Node `tsx` tests.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "GlMAa9eIApW0nsEPkOybEQ"
