  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Elimination**\n\nI\'ve made a breakthrough! Identifying the `FOUND_TODO_BADGE` case was pivotal. The lingering `\"TODO \303\227\"` string in `dist` was perplexing. The change from `import.meta.env.DEV` to `import.meta.env?.DEV` clearly reveals Vite\'s static dead-code elimination and its interaction with how the `import.meta` object is handled. I am now looking at the build step details.\n\n\n**Investigating the Variable**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into how `import.meta.env.DEV` behaves. The core issue seems to be that Vite replaces the literal with `false`, but the optional chaining scenario becomes `false?.DEV`, which isn\'t always eliminated. This means exploring how to refactor `DevTodoBadge.tsx` and other files to ensure complete removal during the build, without runtime issues in Node. I\'m considering using `typeof import.meta !== \"undefined\" && import.meta.env && import.meta.env.DEV`, but I need to test how Vite handles this.\n\n\n"
