  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Vite\'s Behavior**\n\nI\'ve been examining the Vite configuration, specifically the `DevTodoBadge.tsx` file. Line 6, using optional chaining with `import.meta.env?.DEV`, presents an interesting case. It seems the optional chaining within Vite prevents the `define` plugin from directly rewriting the conditional during the build process, which has some implications on expected behavior in different environments.\n\n\n**Investigating Vite\'s Optimizations**\n\nI\'ve discovered Vite aggressively constant-folds `import.meta.env.DEV` to `false` directly, which has significant impact. I am testing `if (!import.meta.env.DEV)` and `Boolean(import.meta.env && import.meta.env.DEV)` to observe these behavior changes, and it seems this constant folding will be applied to those expressions as well! I\'m also examining the `IslandCanvas` chunk size to optimize it further, as it\'s slightly over the target gzipped size.\n\n\n"
