  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing StoryVine Placement**\n\nOkay, so I\'ve pinpointed the `StoryVine` overlap. It\'s in `Story.tsx` where `StoryVine` has `fixed right-5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2`. The placement isn\'t happening because it is outside of `max-w-7xl`, but I need to investigate the implications of `fixed` inside a transformed container. The `stageRef` is pinned with `transform`, so this may resolve the issue. Now, I have more information to follow up on.\n\n\n**Investigating Edge Placement**\n\nOkay, I\'ve dug into the positioning at the 1440px viewport. I\'ve calculated the `max-w-7xl` edge, the right margin, and now I\'m chasing why the StoryVine is overlapping the card in the image. I was honing in on `lg:right-28` within `Story.tsx`, figuring it was the culprit, but now I see the card\'s right edge in the image is off. The issue is with the actual pixel measurements in the image. The values in the image do not align with my calculations of the position of StoryVine, I need to check the math.\n\n\n**Clarifying Overlap Positioning**\n\nOkay, I\'ve had a breakthrough! It appears I was on the right track with `Story.tsx` line 432. I now understand why the card\'s position was off. The combination of `inset-x-*` (which translates to `inset-inline-*`) and the use of `left` and `right` with `lg:` within the same element created the issue. I was able to pinpoint how `inset-inline-end` differs from physical `right`, which was my key discovery. I believe the physical right is overriding the logical properties. I\'m going to follow this direction.\n\n\n**Verifying New Approaches**\n\nI\'m verifying two fixes right now. I\'ve re-evaluated the `StoryVine` issue and the card\'s right border, realizing the vine\'s overlap is unnecessary. If I replace `lg:right-28` with `lg:inset-x-8 xl:inset-x-10 lg:pr-24`, it will never overlap the cards. Also, using `md:right-28 lg:right-32` and `lg:pr-24` will solve the problem. I\'m measuring and testing the values right now to ensure accurate placement.\n\n\n**Refining Card Positioning**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a cleaner solution. By setting the card wrapper\'s class to `absolute inset-x-4 sm:inset-x-6 lg:inset-x-8 lg:pr-24 bottom-3 md:bottom-auto md:top-1/2 md:-translate-y-1/2`, I eliminate the ambiguity of physical-vs-logical properties. This guarantees enough clearance for StoryVine at all desktop widths. I\'m also considering spacing to prevent collision, not pills. I am ready to test my changes.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "qVYAa7KrA4aHxs0PxJCL2AM"
