  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Fixing StoryVine Placement**\n\nI\'ve tackled that `StoryVine` issue and got it squared away. It\'s now fixed within the GSAP pin container of `stageRef`, so it doesn\'t leak into `PlansHighlight`. Using absolute positioning, `absolute right-5 top-1/2 -translate-y-1/2`, makes sure it stays put even when GSAP changes the positioning.\n\n\n**Analyzing Annotation Placement**\n\nI\'m now examining the positioning of annotations within `story-shield.png`. In `Story.tsx`, `handleProjectAnchors` logic has become clearer, differentiating between left and right-side cards, and I\'ve started to map the horizontal placement of `ChapterCard` within the container, taking into account `max-w-7xl`, margins, and inner content width for different screen sizes, specifically focusing on a 1440px desktop width. I\'m now honing in on the horizontal coordinate ranges for left and right cards on desktop.\n\n\n**Refining Anchor Horizontal Bounds**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on defining precise horizontal boundaries for annotation placement, specifically on desktop. My focus is on calculating `minLx` and `maxLx` values. My goal is to ensure that, for the left card, the annotation doesn\'t overlap the right card. I\'m taking into account margins, box widths, and inner content widths, aiming for accurate, non-overlapping placement. My goal is to prevent overlap with right-side cards, making sure everything is clear.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "vVYAa66ZJ6uwnsEP4rL-qAY"
    tool_calls {
