    thinking: "**Discovering Connections**\n\nNow I see it! The cream band at the top of `story-shield.png`? It\'s linked to `Story.tsx` line 150, but hold on, not directly. It\'s a `Canvas`. I need to figure out how this `Canvas` setting impacts the image output!\n\n\n**Pinpointing the Cause**\n\nI\'ve got it! The cream band in the image? It\'s not the `stageRef`, it\'s the result of the `ScrollTrigger` pin on the `stageRef`. The cream is the `pinSpacer` being inserted. I\'m focusing on why the `Canvas` is effectively offset by ~112px because of the `pinSpacer` from ScrollTrigger. This is why the cream band!\n\n\n**Analyzing the Layering**\n\nOkay, the puzzle deepens. I\'m now wrestling with why the top 112px is cream (#FAF6EC) and the rest is a light warm-gray (#E8E3E2). I am looking across the whole width at y=112px. It\'s a flat horizontal line! Is something in `IslandCanvas.tsx`, `CameraRig.tsx`, or `PostFX.tsx` setting backgrounds or fog? No, and not the `<Nav>`, as it translates away. I am investigating why `Seed` in `StoryVine` (at y = ~460) makes `stageRef` 0..900. I am rechecking `story-neighbors.png`, which didn\'t have the cream bar!\n\n\n**Unraveling the Offset**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the root cause. I\'ve realized `stageRef` was pushed down 112px in the viewport. This is due to a negative value. Further analysis of `SmoothScroll.tsx`, specifically the `ScrollTrigger` logic, is key. I am checking the `start` and `end` values that determine the pushing. I\'m focused on the calculations that result in this vertical offset and why it\'s specific to the story-shield image.\n\n\n**Investigating the Discrepancy**\n\nOkay, I\'m stuck on why `stageRef` was at `y = +112` in `story-shield.png`. I\'m going through `Story.tsx` again. I\'m focusing on the `Nav` element, the `Lenis` scroll, and the interaction of `ScrollTrigger`. I\'m starting to think I was too quick to rule out padding. I\'m checking `Home.tsx` to see if there\'s any pre-existing offset before the story page is loaded. Now I see I missed the root cause.\n\n\n"
