  planner_response {
    response: "Built the marketing website for **Petalnode** following the sketchbook aesthetic and storyboard specifications.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n- **Content & Release Guardrails**:\n  - Central typed content store holding all site copy, plan tiers, hardware specs, FAQ items, navigation, footer data, and explicit `TODO` placeholders without inventing prices, specs, URLs, or reviews.\n  - Release check script (`npm run check:release`) reporting remaining `TODO` placeholders before deployment.\n  - Development-only `TODO` counter badge and dev inspection routes (`/dev/sketch`, `/dev/textures`), stripped from production builds.\n\n- **Sketch UI Kit & Layout**:\n  - Custom hand-drawn component primitives using deterministic `roughjs` geometry (note-card borders, highlighter swashes, wavy underlines, ink arrows, washi tape strips, Polaroid frames, rubber stamps, sticker buttons, SVG boiling filters, pixel-pixelated Nodey & Sprout mascots, and clean line icons).\n  - Sticky hide-on-scroll top bar on desktop and a ruled-paper drawer menu on mobile, paired with the interactive Doodle Crew footer displaying the giant dry-brush **PETALNODE** wordmark, six reactive characters (`Nodey`, `Pip`, `Morel`, `Sprout`, `Boo`, `Patch`), drifting doodles, and the Mojang disclaimer.\n\n- **Interactive 3D Island Scroll Story (`/`)**:\n  - Deterministic procedural floating cherry-blossom voxel island (~4,600 blocks) with procedural 64\303\22764 pixel-art materials and a custom WebGL post-processing shader that transitions the island smoothly from cross-hatched ink-on-cream sketch to sunlit full color and dusk lanterns across scroll progress (`0` to `1`).\n  - Six pinned, reversible scrubbed chapters (**Seed**, **Roots**, **Shield**, **Instant Build**, **Neighbors**, **Bloom**) with live camera choreography, interactive **StoryVine** chapter navigation, live 3D-to-screen projected ink annotations, animated loader panel preview, Bloom Polaroid shrink-and-snapshot transition, and a full static SVG fallback (`?static=1`, reduced motion, or no WebGL).\n\n- **Landing, Plans & Fallback Pages**:\n  - **Home (`/`)**: Interactive/static story, highlighted 3-plan section (`Sprout`, `Sapling` marked `OUR PICK`, `Blossom`) with the frozen Bloom snapshot Polaroid, trust strip, expandable FAQ accordion, and final CTA.\n  - **Plans (`/plans`)**: All six tiers (`Seed`, `Sprout`, `Sapling`, `Blossom`, `Grove`, `Orchard`), responsive ruled-notebook comparison table with a sticky feature column on mobile, and the Plans FAQ subset.\n  - **404 (`/*`)**: Hand-drawn Nodey and wilted Sprout illustration with a return-home link.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit & SSR Tests**: 42/42 passing across content validation, quality tiering, story range math, deterministic rough paths, procedural island & texture generation, footer behavior, and component SSR rendering.\n- **Typecheck & Build**: TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with 0 errors, applet compilation succeeded, and production Vite bundling verified clean tree-shaking of dev-only routes and the dev badge.\n- **Headless Browser Verification**: Tested desktop interactive scrolling, StoryVine jumps, annotation/card spacing, footer storyboard reveal, `?static=1` fallback, `/plans`, `/missing-page` 404, and mobile `390\303\227844` layout with zero console errors or horizontal overflow."
    message_id: "f1kAa4XCOt-G28oPhs6nmAE"
    modified_response: "Built the marketing website for **Petalnode** following the sketchbook aesthetic and storyboard specifications.\n\n### Key Features Implemented\n- **Content & Release Guardrails**:\n  - Central typed content store holding all site copy, plan tiers, hardware specs, FAQ items, navigation, footer data, and explicit `TODO` placeholders without inventing prices, specs, URLs, or reviews.\n  - Release check script (`npm run check:release`) reporting remaining `TODO` placeholders before deployment.\n  - Development-only `TODO` counter badge and dev inspection routes (`/dev/sketch`, `/dev/textures`), stripped from production builds.\n\n- **Sketch UI Kit & Layout**:\n  - Custom hand-drawn component primitives using deterministic `roughjs` geometry (note-card borders, highlighter swashes, wavy underlines, ink arrows, washi tape strips, Polaroid frames, rubber stamps, sticker buttons, SVG boiling filters, pixel-pixelated Nodey & Sprout mascots, and clean line icons).\n  - Sticky hide-on-scroll top bar on desktop and a ruled-paper drawer menu on mobile, paired with the interactive Doodle Crew footer displaying the giant dry-brush **PETALNODE** wordmark, six reactive characters (`Nodey`, `Pip`, `Morel`, `Sprout`, `Boo`, `Patch`), drifting doodles, and the Mojang disclaimer.\n\n- **Interactive 3D Island Scroll Story (`/`)**:\n  - Deterministic procedural floating cherry-blossom voxel island (~4,600 blocks) with procedural 64\303\22764 pixel-art materials and a custom WebGL post-processing shader that transitions the island smoothly from cross-hatched ink-on-cream sketch to sunlit full color and dusk lanterns across scroll progress (`0` to `1`).\n  - Six pinned, reversible scrubbed chapters (**Seed**, **Roots**, **Shield**, **Instant Build**, **Neighbors**, **Bloom**) with live camera choreography, interactive **StoryVine** chapter navigation, live 3D-to-screen projected ink annotations, animated loader panel preview, Bloom Polaroid shrink-and-snapshot transition, and a full static SVG fallback (`?static=1`, reduced motion, or no WebGL).\n\n- **Landing, Plans & Fallback Pages**:\n  - **Home (`/`)**: Interactive/static story, highlighted 3-plan section (`Sprout`, `Sapling` marked `OUR PICK`, `Blossom`) with the frozen Bloom snapshot Polaroid, trust strip, expandable FAQ accordion, and final CTA.\n  - **Plans (`/plans`)**: All six tiers (`Seed`, `Sprout`, `Sapling`, `Blossom`, `Grove`, `Orchard`), responsive ruled-notebook comparison table with a sticky feature column on mobile, and the Plans FAQ subset.\n  - **404 (`/*`)**: Hand-drawn Nodey and wilted Sprout illustration with a return-home link.\n\n### Verification Summary\n- **Unit & SSR Tests**: 42/42 passing across content validation, quality tiering, story range math, deterministic rough paths, procedural island & texture generation, footer behavior, and component SSR rendering.\n- **Typecheck & Build**: TypeScript (`tsc --noEmit`) passed with 0 errors, applet compilation succeeded, and production Vite bundling verified clean tree-shaking of dev-only routes and the dev badge.\n- **Headless Browser Verification**: Tested desktop interactive scrolling, StoryVine jumps, annotation/card spacing, footer storyboard reveal, `?static=1` fallback, `/plans`, `/missing-page` 404, and mobile `390\303\227844` layout with zero console errors or horizontal overflow."
