    thinking: "**Defining Brand Attributes**\n\nI\'m focused on solidifying the brand\'s core elements. Section 1 is crucial: I\'m making sure `Brand` is \"Petalnodes\", and `Main Website` links to `https://petalnodes.cloud`, exactly as outlined. I am carefully cross-referencing this to `metadata.json` which must not be renamed! I am confident with the fundamentals.\n\n\n**Mapping Digital Ecosystem**\n\nI\'m now mapping out all the digital touchpoints. I\'ve got the billing portal and client area as `https://billing.petalnodes.cloud`, game panel as `https://panel.petalnodes.cloud`, and Discord set to `https://discord.gg/GS3wuc4HGk`. The status page is `https://status.petalnodes.cloud`. Social media links are a bit tricky, though. I\'m noting YouTube as `TODO: YouTube URL` since it is unverified, and the same applies to X.\n\n\n**Refining Social Integrations**\n\nI\'ve got the verified YouTube URL in place, and I\'m marking X and Instagram as \"TODO\" for later owner confirmation. TikTok is completely removed. I\'ve updated the footer config to filter out the unverified social links for now. Now, I\'m auditing the Master Prompt to design a clean implementation across Phases 2-7, seeking zero regressions.\n\n\n**Defining Site Routes**\n\nI\'ve established all core site URLs including docs, terms, privacy, and other essential pages as first-class routes for complete internal linking. I\'ve reconfirmed the site, store, client, game panel, discord, and status page URLs. Social media links are set. The plan is to configure YouTube, X, and Instagram, and I\'m ensuring no TikTok appears anywhere. I\'ll need to remove any existing placeholder text to configure YouTube, X, and Instagram.\n\n\n**Enumerating Server Plans**\n\nI\'m now detailing the Minecraft hosting plans. I\'m focusing on the exact \"Cherry Blossom\" naming convention, memory, CPU allocation, storage, monthly price, and placeholder payment URLs for each of the seven plans. The \"Sapling\" plan has a special `ourPick: true` attribute. Each entry\'s details are precise and complete.\n\n\n**Detailing Plan Specifications**\n\nI am now meticulously outlining the \"Sakura\" Minecraft hosting plan, focusing on its specific attributes: 24 GB RAM, 600% CPU allocation, 65 GB storage, and a monthly price of \342\202\271449, with a placeholder for the payment URL. I\'m also updating the `PlanId` union type to include \"sakura\" and updating plan-related UI components to handle this new plan. I\'ve updated the \"See all plans\" label to accurately reflect the seven available options and carefully curated plan inclusions to match Minecraft specs, noting the exclusion of Forge and NeoForge. I\'ve moved on to drafting the VPS hosting plans.\n\n\n**Formulating VPS Plans**\n\nI\'ve just detailed the initial VPS hosting plans. I\'ve got the base plan at 8 GB RAM, 3 vCPU, 40 GB NVMe for \342\202\271800. I am not inventing `ourPick`, I am ensuring clean, equal card layouts. I\'m also finalizing `canopy` and `evergrove` with their specs and placeholder payment URLs. I\'m focusing on defining the VPS inclusions and infrastructure details.\n\n\n**Defining Discord Promotions**\n\nI\'m now detailing the Discord promotion specs. I\'ve broken down invite rewards into multiple tiers, from `Petal I` at 2GB RAM up to `Petal VI` at 17GB RAM. Rules for member leave, rejoin, fake accounts, and mass pings, and also the claiming of rewards via Discord are now defined. Also included are boost rewards, from `Bloom I` at 3GB RAM up to `Bloom IV` at 12GB RAM, detailing the Java & Bedrock spec. Lastly I\'ve introduced bot hosting plan suggestions.\n\n\n**Refining Homepage Design**\n\nI\'m now detailing the \"Story Chapters\" section. I\'ve updated Chapter 1 with processor, storage, and memory specs. I have a TODO on network speed. Chapter 2 is locked in with DDoS & Cloudflare protection for every plan. I confirmed the loaders in Chapter 3 for Paper, Purpur, and Fabric, removing the unverified Forge and NeoForge. Also, I updated the description, clarifying the setup and support. I\'m focusing on the PanelSketch, TrustStrip and FAQs.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Component Details**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the game panel URL is factual. I\'m ensuring `PanelSketch.tsx` handles loaders correctly and not with hardcoded values. In Chapter 4, I\'ve updated the specs for support, pricing, and locations. The trust strip now has Ryzen & Xeon Gold, DDR5, locations, protection, and daily backups. I am keeping the review section for later real data. I have begun updating FAQs.\n\n\n**Finalizing FAQs**\n\nI\'ve just added several FAQs to the list. I\'ve defined questions and answers on server provisioning speed, supported software (including Java/Bedrock and Paper, Purpur, Fabric), upgrade paths, DDoS protection, server locations, support channels (Discord and client area), and am currently writing on refund policy and am preparing to finalize these and other existing questions.\n\n\n**Structuring Site Content**\n\nI\'ve just structured all the site\'s content cleanly in `/src/content/`, with a central module at `/src/content/index.ts`. This includes locations, docs, legal drafts, contact, about, and modpacks.\n\n\n**Designing Site Architecture**\n\nI\'m now detailing all the site\'s routes. The new routes I\'ve mapped out are `/vps`, `/bots`, `/locations`, and `/docs`, each with its corresponding component. The `/vps` route will have VPS hosting plans, including `Root`, `Branch`, `Trunk`, `Canopy`, and `Evergrove` specifications. The `/bots` route will focus on dedicated bot hosting, marked as a draft until the specs are defined. The `/locations` route will visually showcase server locations. The `/docs` route will be an interactive knowledge base with filtering and search. Also I\'ll ensure updates on each page\'s `<title>`, meta tags, and JSON-LD data.\n\n\n**Defining Content Framework**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a clear documentation strategy. I\'m building `/modpacks` which addresses file management and server software, clearly focusing on the established Paper/Purpur/Fabric workflow, and documenting the file uploads, and marking unverified modpacks as a `TODO`. I\'m also preparing `/about` which will detail our philosophy, infrastructure and our community-first approach and documenting Discord support. I\'m focusing on `/contact` with Discord support and billing.\n\n\n**Structuring Site Nav**\n\nI\'ve organized the navigation exactly as required, ensuring clear links for home, Minecraft plans, VPS, bot hosting, server locations, documentation, Discord, and the client area. The footer is also up to date, with a prominent draft banner on all legal documents, with `[TODO]` markers where owner sign-off is needed. I am not inventing any legal commitments, ensuring precise adherence to the initial guidelines.\n\n\n**Refining Site Navigation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on optimizing the site\'s navigation, specifically the header and footer. I\'m ensuring the desktop header elements fit cleanly without wrapping, with the `gap-4` to `gap-6` and `text-sm` for responsive design. I\'ve structured the footer to include all the requested links across columns, including `Hosting`, `Resources`, `Company`, and `Account` sections, as per the spec. I\'m ensuring full accuracy.\n\n\n**Implementing Texture Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing the texture improvements, ensuring deterministic outputs with the `paintBlockBuffers` function. I\'m focusing on rich, layered materials within the 64x64 resolution and ensuring nearest-neighbor crisp pixels. I\'m leveraging multi-octave noise, Voronoi speckles, directional scratches, and edge effects. I\'m also addressing alpha cutouts in `cherry_leaves`, while I\'m keeping the test green! I\'m creating roughness/normal maps.\n\n\n**Detailing Texture Refinement**\n\nI\'m now implementing the refined textures with specific effects. I\'m applying sunlit blossom tips, rose shadow pockets, twig flecks, and stipple height. I\'m focusing on realistic bark plates with fissures, and warm heartwood rings for `cherry_log`. I\'m making plank offsets, color shifts, peg nails and bevels for `cherry_planks`. I\'m ensuring organic clumped moss blades, pebbles, and cherry blossoms are in place for `grass`.\n\n\n**Enhancing Texture Inspection**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed inspection into `/src/pages/DevTextures.tsx`. I\'m focused on 3D spinning, lit blocks for each material, alongside their 64x64 Albedo and Normal maps. I will add face breakdowns, including top, side, and bottom views. An interactive light angle and flat-vs-textured checks will be implemented. I\'ll maintain the focus on each material\'s details.\n\n\n**Auditing Button Component**\n\nI\'m now fully auditing the existing React button component, `StickerButton.tsx`, to integrate all required interactive features. I\'m focusing on hover animations, touch feedback, accessible focus states, keyboard interactions, variants, disabled states, and loading states, along with integrating React Router links. I\'m focusing on ensuring it completely supports all interactive capabilities.\n\n\n**Implementing SEO Optimizations**\n\nI\'m now integrating SEO improvements. I am cleanly updating `/index.html` with title, meta descriptions, and Open Graph tags, including structured data. I am creating a `<RouteMeta>` helper in `App.tsx` that will handle dynamic updates to page titles, descriptions, and canonical links for every route, including `/plans`, `/vps`, and all other essential pages, ensuring each has tailored SEO data.\n\n\n"
