s`, `/vps`, `/bots`, `/locations`, `/docs`, `/modpacks`, `/about`, `/contact`, `/terms`, `/privacy`, `/sla`, and dev `/dev/textures`, verifying `0` console/page errors, `0` horizontal overflow, clean visual screenshots (inspect key screenshots via `view_file`), then delete `.playwright-verify` and `.playwright-cli`.\n6. **Phase 8 \342\200\224 Final Report & First Owner Question**:\n   - Present the complete 15-point Final Report specified in section 13.\n   - Ask **EXACTLY ONE clear question** for the first remaining business TODO (e.g., Seed / Minecraft checkout URLs on Paymenter, prioritized per section 11 #1).\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Never invent prices, specs, hardware models/generations, network speeds, backup retention days, uptime SLAs, refund terms, emails, phone numbers, reviews, Forge/NeoForge support, or pre-made modpacks.\n- Keep all outdated names (`Dirt`, `Stone`, `Lapis`, `Diamond`, `Netherite`, `Warden`, `Dragon`, `Starter`, `Basic`, `Pro`, `Advanced`, `Ultimate`) absent from active hosting tiers/UI.\n- Keep `\"Not an official Minecraft product. Not approved by or associated with Mojang or Microsoft.\"` intact in footer.\n- Do not display TikTok; hide unverified social links (`isTodo`).\n- Follow sketchbook visual language strictly (paper/ink/blossom/moss/wood, zero glassmorphism, zero dark neon, zero purple SaaS gradients, zero stock images, zero emoji feature icons, zero forbidden AI words).\n- Only report verified results after all final edits; ask only ONE question at a time in Phase 8.\n</summary>"
