  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Conundrum**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the conflicting clues from the screenshots! The `DevTodoBadge` displaying despite the `/dev/textures` 404 is the primary anomaly. Now, I\'m carefully reviewing `App.tsx`, lines 12-17, as I attempt to connect these dots and identify the root cause of this strange behavior.\n\n\n**Unraveling the Mystery**\n\nI\'ve hit a breakthrough! The crucial detail lies within `App.tsx` and the absence of `/dev/textures` in `ROUTE_META`. This explains the \"Page Not Found\" title. The lazy loading of `@/pages/DevTextures`, a hefty chunk, during the timeout period further complicates things. This absence explains why `h1: null`! Now, I am exploring how the lazy loading interacts with the route definition.\n\n\n**Confirming the Hypothesis**\n\nI\'ve got it! Adding `/dev/textures` and `/dev/sketch` to `ROUTE_META` is key, ensuring the correct rendering and preventing the \"Page Not Found\" title. The Playwright waiting for `h1` will confirm it\'s now rendering fully.\n\nNext, I am digging into the horizontal overflow issues on `/plans` and `/bots`. It seems `CompareTable.tsx` or `RewardsSection.tsx` on `/plans` may have an element exceeding 390px, specifically a potential suspect in `RewardsSection.tsx` line 132 or elements inside `CompareTable.tsx` or `PlanCard.tsx`.\n\n\n"
