  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Error**\n\nI\'m currently focusing on a TypeError related to setting a property (\"fetch\") on a Window object. The error message indicates this property has only a getter. I\'m exploring the context within the extension\'s request interception logic to pinpoint the specific point where this illegal assignment is attempted, as it\'s likely causing a conflict with the expected behavior of the Window object.\n\n\n**Investigating the Cause**\n\nI\'ve traced the TypeError to a Chrome extension attempting to overwrite `window.fetch`. It appears a Proxy/VPN or similar extension is trying to monkey-patch `window.fetch` at `document_start`, leading to the error \"Cannot set property fetch\". Current Chrome environments, especially within iframes or with strict Window objects, define `window.fetch` with a getter, but no setter. I\'m checking our codebase to confirm we\'re not inadvertently modifying `window.fetch`.\n\n\n"
