  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Source**\n\nI\'m currently investigating the root cause of the issue, focusing on how a Chrome extension affects our app\'s behavior. I\'ve pinpointed a specific JavaScript file (`requests.js`) within the extension\'s context that\'s running within the user\'s browser, which seems key to understanding the problem. My goal is to determine if we can gracefully handle the issue without changing our core app code.\n\n\n**Isolating the Conflict**\n\nI\'ve confirmed the issue\'s source: a Chrome extension injecting scripts before our page scripts. The stack traces reveal zero frames from our app, pointing to the extension. In a clean browser profile, without the extension, everything loads error-free. The root cause is likely the extension trying to overwrite `window.fetch`, which is defined as a read-only getter.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "DYcAa_P2MeL8-sAPuPfM0QY"
