  planner_response {
    response: "The procedural 3D material system (`src/three/island/textures.ts`, `src/three/island/IslandBlocks.tsx`, and `/dev/textures`) has been reviewed, upgraded, and verified:\n\n### Key Findings & Upgrades\n\n1. **Corrected Normal Map & UV Orientation**\n   - Fixed `THREE.DataTexture` `flipY = true` alignment so top texture rows (`grass` mossy overhang, `flower` & `sapling` tops) render upright on 3D cubes instead of upside-down.\n   - Aligned the 3\303\2273 seamless Sobel tangent-space normal Y polarity (`ny = +sobelY`) with `flipY = true` so overhead directional lighting catches top stone bevels, plank chamfers, and bark ridges accurately instead of inverting shadows.\n\n2. **PBR Surface Realism Across All 14 Block Types**\n   - **Normal + Roughness Maps:** Replaced uniform roughness values with per-pixel paired `roughnessMap` and 3\303\2273 wrapped Sobel `normalMap` buffers (`64\303\22764` deterministic `NearestFilter` + mipmaps) so stone crevices, soil clods, and bark furrows stay matte while crystal ore facets, water caustics, and polished plank bevels catch specular light.\n   - **Surface Imperfections & Sketchbook Palette Tuning:**\n     - **Stone & Deep Stone:** Periodic Worley cellular masonry fractures, sedimentary strata bands, hairline crevice veins, and chamfered top-left highlights.\n     - **Cherry Bark & Planks:** Cinnamon-brown furrowed bark with horizontal cherry lenticel bands and concentric heartwood/sapwood rings; staggered running-bond planks with wood knots, grain warp, and end-peg accents.\n     - **Grass, Dirt, Path & Moss:** Stratified loamy soil, rootlet fibers, organic warm pebbles, rounded path cobbles, moss tufts, and scattered sakura petals.\n     - **Cherry Leaves & Glow Ore:** Removed muddy dark cutout edges in favor of plum-rose to blush sakura petal rosettes (`~23%` alpha cutouts), and framed gold/pink faceted `glow_ore` crystals inside dark slate sockets with balanced `emissiveIntensity`.\n\n3. **Performance & Art-Direction Compatibility**\n   - **Quality-Tier PBR Scaling:** `high` tier enables full `albedo + normalMap + roughnessMap`, `medium` keeps `albedo + normalMap`, and `low` / mobile falls back to lightweight single-albedo shading.\n   - **Zero-Cost Instance Variation:** Added deterministic GPU per-instance tinting (`InstancedMesh.setColorAt`) across `cherry_leaves`, `grass`, `dirt`, `stone`, `deep_stone`, `cherry_planks`, and `moss_carpet` with zero extra draw calls or textures.\n   - **Sketchbook Integration:** Tuned `envMapIntensity` per material so `RoomEnvironment` reflections never wash out `SketchEffect` ink outlines and cross-hatching.\n\n### Verification\n\n- **Unit & Shader Tests:** **38 / 38 passing** (`textures.test.ts`, `islandGenerator.test.ts`, `content.test.ts`, `sections.test.tsx`, `doodle-crew-footer.test.ts`), including deterministic PBR buffers, alpha cutouts, and tangent-space normal Y polarity assertions.\n- **Compilation & Lint:** `compile_applet` and `tsc --noEmit` succeeded with 0 errors.\n- **Headless Chromium Visual Audit:** Inspected all 14 blocks on `/dev/textures` (High/Medium/Low tiers + Daylight/Sunset/Lantern modes) and the `/` WebGL hero/sketchbook render with **0 console or page errors**."
    message_id: "OogAa6fOB-iP6dkP2qD_oA4"
    modified_response: "The procedural 3D material system (`src/three/island/textures.ts`, `src/three/island/IslandBlocks.tsx`, and `/dev/textures`) has been reviewed, upgraded, and verified:\n\n### Key Findings & Upgrades\n\n1. **Corrected Normal Map & UV Orientation**\n   - Fixed `THREE.DataTexture` `flipY = true` alignment so top texture rows (`grass` mossy overhang, `flower` & `sapling` tops) render upright on 3D cubes instead of upside-down.\n   - Aligned the 3\303\2273 seamless Sobel tangent-space normal Y polarity (`ny = +sobelY`) with `flipY = true` so overhead directional lighting catches top stone bevels, plank chamfers, and bark ridges accurately instead of inverting shadows.\n\n2. **PBR Surface Realism Across All 14 Block Types**\n   - **Normal + Roughness Maps:** Replaced uniform roughness values with per-pixel paired `roughnessMap` and 3\303\2273 wrapped Sobel `normalMap` buffers (`64\303\22764` deterministic `NearestFilter` + mipmaps) so stone crevices, soil clods, and bark furrows stay matte while crystal ore facets, water caustics, and polished plank bevels catch specular light.\n   - **Surface Imperfections & Sketchbook Palette Tuning:**\n     - **Stone & Deep Stone:** Periodic Worley cellular masonry fractures, sedimentary strata bands, hairline crevice veins, and chamfered top-left highlights.\n     - **Cherry Bark & Planks:** Cinnamon-brown furrowed bark with horizontal cherry lenticel bands and concentric heartwood/sapwood rings; staggered running-bond planks with wood knots, grain warp, and end-peg accents.\n     - **Grass, Dirt, Path & Moss:** Stratified loamy soil, rootlet fibers, organic warm pebbles, rounded path cobbles, moss tufts, and scattered sakura petals.\n     - **Cherry Leaves & Glow Ore:** Removed muddy dark cutout edges in favor of plum-rose to blush sakura petal rosettes (`~23%` alpha cutouts), and framed gold/pink faceted `glow_ore` crystals inside dark slate sockets with balanced `emissiveIntensity`.\n\n3. **Performance & Art-Direction Compatibility**\n   - **Quality-Tier PBR Scaling:** `high` tier enables full `albedo + normalMap + roughnessMap`, `medium` keeps `albedo + normalMap`, and `low` / mobile falls back to lightweight single-albedo shading.\n   - **Zero-Cost Instance Variation:** Added deterministic GPU per-instance tinting (`InstancedMesh.setColorAt`) across `cherry_leaves`, `grass`, `dirt`, `stone`, `deep_stone`, `cherry_planks`, and `moss_carpet` with zero extra draw calls or textures.\n   - **Sketchbook Integration:** Tuned `envMapIntensity` per material so `RoomEnvironment` reflections never wash out `SketchEffect` ink outlines and cross-hatching.\n\n### Verification\n\n- **Unit & Shader Tests:** **38 / 38 passing** (`textures.test.ts`, `islandGenerator.test.ts`, `content.test.ts`, `sections.test.tsx`, `doodle-crew-footer.test.ts`), including deterministic PBR buffers, alpha cutouts, and tangent-space normal Y polarity assertions.\n- **Compilation & Lint:** `compile_applet` and `tsc --noEmit` succeeded with 0 errors.\n- **Headless Chromium Visual Audit:** Inspected all 14 blocks on `/dev/textures` (High/Medium/Low tiers + Daylight/Sunset/Lantern modes) and the `/` WebGL hero/sketchbook render with **0 console or page errors**."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
