    session_summary: "<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\nContinuing development on the **Petalnodes** React + Vite + Three.js (`@react-three/fiber` + `@react-three/postprocessing`) application.\n\n### Current Active Request\nUpdate the procedural voxel material pipeline and `/dev/textures` inspector page to:\n1. **Update `/dev/textures` (`/src/pages/DevTextures.tsx`)** to display:\n   - **Side-by-side comparisons** of the **Original (Flat)** vs. **Improved Normal + Height-Mapped (PBR)** procedural voxel block materials.\n   - An interactive **toggle for surface grain intensity** (e.g., `Subtle (0.5\303\227)` / `Balanced (1.0\303\227)` / `Rich (1.8\303\227)` or slider/buttons) that dynamically updates 3D block materials and 2D texture channel swatches.\n2. **Integrate height map generation** into the procedural material pipeline (`src/three/island/textures.ts`) specifically for **`stone`** (and `deep_stone`) and **`bark` (`cherry_log`)** textures to improve crevice depth and lighting response without external assets.\n3. Ensure desktop/mobile performance, quality-tier compatibility, and full compatibility with the existing sketchbook art direction (`SketchEffect` outlines/cross-hatching, `IslandBlocks` instancing, `RoomEnvironment`).\n\n*(Note from earlier session turns: Core site pages, Cherry Blossom 7-tier Minecraft plans, 5-tier VPS plans, Petal/Bloom rewards, 10 new routes, SEO/JSON-LD, `StickerButton`, and unit/SSR tests were previously completed and verified, awaiting owner Paymenter URLs when they return to TODO collection.)*\n\n## 2. Progress\n### Skills Already Read\n- `ultra-mode`, `frontend-design`, `threejs`, `computer-use` (`playwright-cli` rules & container flags), `applet-seo`.\n\n### Completed for Current Request (UNCOMPILED / UNTESTED AFTER LATEST EDIT)\n1. **Verified Three.js `0.187.0` Native UV Channel `0` `aoMap` Support**:\n   - Checked `node_modules/@types/three/src/textures/Texture.d.ts` and `node_modules/three/src/renderers/shaders/ShaderChunk/aomap_fragment.glsl.js`.\n   - Confirmed `THREE.DataTexture.channel = 0` allows `MeshStandardMaterial.aoMap` to sample `heightMap` on `BoxGeometry`\'s default UV channel `0` with zero geometry changes or custom GLSL risk.\n2. **Upgraded `/src/three/island/textures.ts`** (written, NOT YET compiled/tested):\n   - Exported `MaterialVariant = \"pbr\" | \"flat\"`, `PaintBlockOptions { grainIntensity?: number }`, `MaterialOptions`, `usesHeightMapRelief(type)` (returns `true` for `\"stone\"`, `\"deep_stone\"`, `\"cherry_log\"`), and `paintHeightMap(type, face, options)`.\n   - Added `heightMap: Uint8Array` (`64\303\22764\303\2274` RGBA grayscale buffer) to `PaintedBlockBuffers`.\n   - Enriched `paintBlockBuffers(type, face, options)` with `grainIntensity` (`0..2.5`, default `1.0`) scaling micro-grain imperfections, `stone` mineral pitting/strata/fissures, `cherry_log` bark fiber striations & deep furrows, roughness contrast, and Sobel normal strength (`baseStrength * (0.45 + 0.55 * grain)`).\n   - Preserved `tex.flipY = true` and corrected Sobel Y polarity (`ny = +sobelY`) so top ridges catch overhead directional light accurately.\n   - Updated `getBlockMaterial(type, tier, attachStory = true, options: MaterialOptions = {})`:\n     - Caches by `${type}:${tier}:${attachStory ? \"story\" : \"plain\"}:${variant}:${grain.toFixed(2)}`.\n     - `\"flat\"` variant: disables `normalMap`, `roughnessMap`, and `aoMap`, uses `grain = 0`, providing an authentic original flat-texture comparison baseline.\n     - `\"pbr\"` variant: attaches `normalMap` (`tier !== \"low\"`), `roughnessMap` (`tier === \"high\"`), AND for `stone`, `deep_stone`, `cherry_log` (`tier !== \"low\"`), attaches `aoMap: heightAoMap` (`channel = 0`, `aoMapIntensity: Math.min(1.15, 0.58 * (0.5 + 0.5 * grain))`) so height maps directly deepen crevice shadowing and lighting response.\n\n### Remaining Uncompleted Work\n1. Update `/src/pages/DevTextures.tsx`.\n2. Add unit tests for height maps, flat vs. PBR variants, and grain intensity in `/src/three/island/textures.test.ts`.\n3. Compile, typecheck, run tests, restart Vite dev server, and run `playwright-cli` visual + console verification on `/dev/textures` and `/`.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n- **Browser WebGL Context Cap (~16 contexts):** Rendering 14 `<Canvas>` cards is already near Chromium\'s 16-context limit. For Side-by-Side mode on `/dev/textures`, render **both cubes (`Original Flat` on left `x = -0.95`, `New Normal+Height PBR` on right `x = +0.95`) inside the SAME `<Canvas>` per block card**, spinning synchronously (`mesh.rotation.y += delta * 0.65`) under identical directional + ambient lighting! That gives all 14 blocks true side-by-side 3D comparison with zero extra WebGL contexts.\n- **`IslandBlocks.tsx` Compatibility:** Calls `getBlockMaterial(type, tier, true)` with 3 args, which seamlessly defaults to `variant: \"pbr\"` and `grainIntensity: 1.0`. Already includes deterministic per-instance tinting (`setColorAt`) with zero extra draw calls.\n- **`textures.test.ts` Existing Invariants (must keep passing):**\n  - 64\303\22764\303\2274 deterministic `albedo`, `normal`, `roughness` buffers.\n  - `cherry_leaves` 15\342\200\22335% transparent cutout pixels (`alpha === 0`).\n  - `glow_ore` > 50 emissive pixels vs `stone` 0 emissive pixels.\n  - `grass` side top 8 rows (`y=0..7`) greener than bottom 8 rows (`y=56..63`).\n  - `stone` normal map `avgZ > 160` & `xMax - xMin > 40`; `cherry_planks` top bevel `G > 128` (`+v` upward).\n\n## 4. Errors & Fixes\n- Earlier resolved in prior turn:\n  - Fixed `DataTexture.flipY` default `false` putting `grass` moss overhang at bottom edge of 3D cubes (`tex.flipY = true` fixed it).\n  - Fixed inverted Sobel `ny` (`-sobelY` -> `+sobelY`) for `flipY = true` UV orientation.\n  - Fixed mobile `390px` horizontal overflow via `overflow-x-clip` on `PaperBackground.tsx`.\n  - Confirmed user\'s `Cannot set property fetch of #<Window>` error came solely from external Chrome extension `eppiocemhmnlbhjplcgkofciiegomcon` (0 occurrences in app code).\n- No errors yet on the new `textures.ts` write \342\200\224 compile/tests have NOT been run yet since modifying `textures.ts`.\n\n## 5. Active Context\n- Workspace: `/app/applet` (dev server runs with `DISABLE_HMR=true` and `watch: null`, so always run `restart_dev_server` after edits before running `playwright-cli`).\n- Modified file in working tree awaiting compilation/tests: `/src/three/island/textures.ts`.\n- Pre-installed headless verification binary: `/usr/local/bin/playwright-cli` (no `.playwright-cli` folder currently exists; clean up `.playwright-cli/` after visual verification).\n\n## 6. Next Steps (Exact Order)\n1. **Update `/src/pages/DevTextures.tsx`**:\n   - Add header controls:\n     - **Compare Mode toggle:** `\"Side-by-Side\"` (default ON \342\200\224 renders Left = `Original (Flat)` vs Right = `New (Normal + Height)` inside each card\'s `<Canvas>`) vs `\"PBR Only\"`.\n     - **Surface Grain Intensity toggle:** `0.5` (`\"Subtle 0.5\303\227\"`), `1.0` (`\"Balanced 1.0\303\227\"`, default), `1.8` (`\"Rich 1.8\303\227\"`).\n     - Keep existing **Quality Tier** (`high` / `medium` / `low`) and **Lighting** (`daylight` / `sunset` / `lantern`) toggles.\n   - Adjust `<Canvas>` camera (`position: compare ? [0, 0.3, 4.1] : [0, 0.25, 3.1]`, `fov: compare ? 38 : 36`) and `<boxGeometry args={[1.22, 1.22, 1.22]} />` when side-by-side (`x = -0.98` for `variant: \"flat\"`, `x = 0.98` for `variant: \"pbr\"` with `grainIntensity`). Add clear compact labels `Flat (Original)` / `PBR (Normal + Height)` below the viewport in side-by-side mode, plus a subtle pill/tag `\"height + normal\"` on `stone`, `deep_stone`, and `cherry_log` cards.\n   - Pass `grainIntensity` to `TextureSwatch` (`side`, `top` for multi-face, `normal`, `rough`, AND `height` channel swatch when `usesHeightMapRelief(type)` is true \342\200\224 i.e., `stone`, `deep_stone`, `cherry_log`!).\n2. **Update `/src/three/island/textures.test.ts`**:\n   - Verify `paintHeightMap(type, \"side\")` returns deterministic `64 * 64 * 4` RGBA buffer and `usesHeightMapRelief` returns `true` for `stone`, `deep_stone`, `cherry_log` and `false` for `water`/`flower`.\n   - Verify `getBlockMaterial(\"stone\", \"high\", false, { variant: \"flat\" })` has `normalMap === null && aoMap === null`, whereas `{ variant: \"pbr\", grainIntensity: 1.0 }` attaches `normalMap`, `roughnessMap`, and `aoMap` (`channel === 0`). Also verify `cherry_log` attaches `aoMap` on its side/top/bottom materials in `pbr` mode.\n   - Verify increasing `grainIntensity` (`0.4` vs `1.8`) measurably changes `paintBlockBuffers(\"stone\", \"side\", ...)` height variance / normal relief.\n3. **Compile, Lint & Test**:\n   - Run `npx --yes tsx --test src/three/island/textures.test.ts src/three/island/islandGenerator.test.ts src/content/content.test.ts src/sections/sections.test.tsx src/components/ui/doodle-crew-footer.test.ts`.\n   - Co-execute `compile_applet`, `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`), and `restart_dev_server`.\n4. **Headless Browser Visual Verification (`playwright-cli`)**:\n   - Open `http://localhost:3000/dev/textures` in headless Chromium (`--browser=chromium`, `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`).\n   - Verify `0` console/page errors, capture side-by-side top & scrolled screenshots (showing `stone`, `cherry_log`, `deep_stone` with `height` swatch and side-by-side cubes), click `Rich 1.8\303\227` grain toggle, and capture `/` home canvas screenshot to verify full compatibility with the sketchbook 3D scene.\n   - Visually inspect attached screenshots cleanly; delete `.playwright-cli/` afterward.\n\n## 7. Commitments & Constraints\n- Use global `playwright-cli` directly (never `npx playwright-cli`, never standalone `playwright` Node scripts), headless Chromium only, `trap \'playwright-cli close\' EXIT`, unique filenames in `.playwright-cli/`.\n- Never invent specs/prices/URLs or alter unrelated verified content/pages.\n- Preserve existing sketchbook visual aesthetic (`#FBF6EE` paper, `#2B2230` ink, `#E2557B`/`#FF8FAB` blossom, `NearestFilter` pixelated 64\303\22764 textures, zero dark neon / zero stock assets).\n- Do NOT break default `getBlockMaterial(type, tier, attachStory)` 3-arg signature used by `IslandBlocks.tsx`.\n</summary>"
