  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Inspecting Key Visuals**\n\nI\'m currently focused on visually inspecting the provided screenshots, specifically `r1-textures-top.png` and `r1-textures-mid.png`. It\'s crucial to closely analyze the layout, cards, side-by-side comparison cubes, and texture swatches, as I believe there are vital, yet subtle details present. My analysis aims to expose potential insights that a cursory review might miss.\n\n\n**Analyzing PBR Darkening**\n\nI\'ve made a crucial observation. The PBR cubes on the right, specifically `stone`, `deep_stone`, and `cherry_log`, appear significantly darker than their flat counterparts on the left. I\'m digging into why. It seems that using the `heightMap` directly as the `aoMap`, with a given `aoMapIntensity`, is darkening the ambient lighting, making the overall look darker. The higher height values are darkening the flat faces. It\'s a trade-off: crisp relief versus the unintended shading.\n\n\n**Refining Cavity Occlusion**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a precise solution for cavity occlusion. The current approach causes excessive darkening, especially evident in `cherry_log`. I\'m thinking of how the height map can drive cavity occlusion without impacting midtones. The ridges and higher points should remain bright, while the crevices smoothly transition to a darker value, potentially 0.25 to 0.45. I also need to find a way to make `cherry_planks` and `grass` have subtle fill. I am aiming for crisp relief without this unintended shading.\n\n\n**Observing Relief Enhancement**\n\nI\'m thrilled with the latest PBR cube observations. The `grass`, `dirt`, `cherry_planks`, `path`, `water`, and `moss_carpet` cubes are stunning. The textures now exhibit remarkable relief, particularly with the chiseled wood of the `cherry_planks` and the shimmering ripples in the `water`. My focus now shifts to refining the `aoMap` curve. By ensuring that ridges maintain a value of 1.0, and only crevices dip, I believe we\'ll achieve cleaner, brighter PBR cubes. I also need to check the recent `eval` failures.\n\n\n**Implementing Cavity Mapping**\n\nI\'m excited to report zero console errors; the warnings are inconsequential. I\'ve also checked the home page 3D island canvas after adjusting the height-to-AO cavity curve for `stone`, `deep_stone`, and `cherry_log`. Now, I\'m inspecting `/src/three/island/textures.ts`, specifically lines 880\342\200\223958, where the `heightAoMap` is built. Instead of directly using the raw `bufs.heightMap`, I\'ll implement a `deriveCavityAoFromHeight()` helper function. This function\'s math maps height values to ambient occlusion, preserving sunlit areas and focusing darkening on crevices.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "WIkAa7TMML6kqtsP96fW0A4"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_9644883945308545482"
      name: "multi_replace_file_content"
      arguments_json: "{\"Description\":\"Derive crevice-only AO texture from procedural height field so stone and bark crevices deepen without darkening raised surfaces\", \"Instruction\":\"Add deriveCavityAoFromHeight helper and wire it into getBlockMaterial aoMap for height-relieved blocks\", \"ReplacementChunks\":[{\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":745, \"ReplacementContent\":\"export function paintHeightMap(\\n  type: BlockType,\\n  face: BlockFace = \\\"side\\\",\\n  options?: PaintBlockOptions,\\n): Uint8Array {\\n  return paintBlockBuffers(type, face, options).heightMap;\\n}\\n\\n/**\\n * Converts a normalized [0,1] height field into a crevice-only AO map:\\n * midtones and ridges (h >= 0.56) stay at full 1.0 brightness while\\n * cracks, pits, and bark furrows (h < 0.56) smoothly occlude down to ~0.22.\\n */\\nfunction deriveCavityAoFromHeight(height: Float32Array): Uint8Array {\\n  const out = new Uint8Array(SIZE * SIZE * 4);\\n  for (let i = 0; i < SIZE * SIZE; i++) {\\n    const h = height[i];\\n    const t = clamp01((h - 0.08) / 0.48);\\n    const smooth = t * t * (3 - 2 * t);\\n    const ao = clampByte((0.22 + 0.78 * smooth) * 255);\\n    const p4 = i * 4;\\n    out[p4] = ao;\\n    out[p4 + 1] = ao;\\n    out[p4 + 2] = ao;\\n    out[p4 + 3] = 255;\\n  }\\n  return out;\\n}\", \"StartLine\":735, \"TargetContent\":\"export function paintHeightMap(\\n  type: BlockType,\\n  face: BlockFace = \\\"side\\\",\\n  options?: PaintBlockOptions,\\n): Uint8Array {\\n  return paintBlockBuffers(type, face, options).heightMap;\\n}\"}, {\"AllowMultiple\":false, \"EndLine\":946, \"ReplacementContent\":\"    const heightAoMap = useHeightCavityMap\\n      ? makeDataTexture(deriveCavityAoFromHeight(bufs.height), false)\\n      : undefined;\\n    const hasEmissive = isOre || isLantern;\\n    const emissiveMap = hasEmissive ? makeDataTexture(bufs.emissive, true) : undefined;\\n\\n    const baseRoughness = isWater\\n      ? 0.14\\n      : isOre\\n        ? 0.55\\n        : type === \\\"cherry_planks\\\"\\n          ? 0.68\\n          : type === \\\"stone\\\" || type === \\\"deep_stone\\\"\\n            ? 0.72\\n            : 0.88;\\n\\n    const envIntensity =\\n      variant === \\\"flat\\\"\\n        ? 0.15\\n        : isWater\\n          ? 1.15\\n          : isOre\\n            ? 0.72\\n            : type === \\\"stone\\\" || type === \\\"deep_stone\\\" || type === \\\"cherry_planks\\\"\\n              ? 0.36\\n              : 0.18;\\n\\n    const normalScaleVal = 0.55 + 0.42 * grain;\\n\\n    const matParams: THREE.MeshStandardMaterialParameters = {\\n      color: 0xffffff,\\n      map,\\n      roughness: useRoughnessMap ? 1.0 : baseRoughness,\\n      metalness: isOre ? 0.14 : 0.0,\\n      envMapIntensity: envIntensity,\\n      alphaTest: isLeafOrPlant ? 0.42 : 0,\\n      transparent: isWater,\\n      opacity: isWater ? 0.84 : 1,\\n      side: isLeafOrPlant ? THREE.DoubleSide : THREE.FrontSide,\\n      emissive: hasEmissive ? new THREE.Color(0xffffff) : new THREE.Color(0x000000),\\n      emissiveIntensity: isOre ? 1.35 : isLantern ? 1.55 : 0,\\n    };\\n    if (normalMap) {\\n      matParams.normalMap = normalMap;\\n      matParams.normalScale = new THREE.Vector2(normalScaleVal, normalScaleVal);\\n    }\\n    if (roughnessMap) {\\n      matParams.roughnessMap = roughnessMap;\\n    }\\n    if (heightAoMap) {\\n      // Height-derived cavity AO deepens stone fissures and bark furrows while keeping ridges bright\\n      matParams.aoMap = heightAoMap;\\n      matParams.aoMapIntensity = Math.min(1.05, 0.62 * (0.45 + 0.55 * grain));\\n    }\", \"StartLine\":892, \"TargetContent\":\"    const heightAoMap = useHeightCavityMap ? makeDataTexture(bufs.heightMap, false) : undefined;\\n    const hasEmissive = isOre || isLantern;\\n    const emissiveMap = hasEmissive ? makeDataTexture(bufs.emissive, true) : undefined;\\n\\n    const baseRoughness = isWater\\n      ? 0.14\\n      : isOre\\n        ? 0.55\\n        : type === \\\"cherry_planks\\\"\\n          ? 0.68\\n          : type === \\\"stone\\\" || type === \\\"deep_stone\\\"\\n            ? 0.72\\n            : 0.88;\\n\\n    const envIntensity =\\n      variant === \\\"flat\\\"\\n        ? 0.15\\n        : isWater\\n          ? 1.15\\n          : isOre\\n            ? 0.72\\n            : type === \\\"stone\\\" || type === \\\"deep_stone\\\" || type === \\\"cherry_planks\\\"\\n              ? 0.36\\n              : 0.18;\\n\\n    const normalScaleVal = 0.55 + 0.42 * grain;\\n\\n    const matParams: THREE.MeshStandardMaterialParameters = {\\n      color: 0xffffff,\\n      map,\\n      roughness: useRoughnessMap ? 1.0 : baseRoughness,\\n      metalness: isOre ? 0.14 : 0.0,\\n      envMapIntensity: envIntensity,\\n      alphaTest: isLeafOrPlant ? 0.42 : 0,\\n      transparent: isWater,\\n      opacity: isWater ? 0.84 : 1,\\n      side: isLeafOrPlant ? THREE.DoubleSide : THREE.FrontSide,\\n      emissive: hasEmissive ? new THREE.Color(0xffffff) : new THREE.Color(0x000000),\\n      emissiveIntensity: isOre ? 1.35 : isLantern ? 1.55 : 0,\\n    };\\n    if (normalMap) {\\n      matParams.normalMap = normalMap;\\n      matParams.normalScale = new THREE.Vector2(normalScaleVal, normalScaleVal);\\n    }\\n    if (roughnessMap) {\\n      matParams.roughnessMap = roughnessMap;\\n    }\\n    if (heightAoMap) {\\n      // Height map wired to UV-channel-0 AO provides crevice self-occlusion on stone and bark\\n      matParams.aoMap = heightAoMap;\\n      matParams.aoMapIntensity = Math.min(1.15, 0.58 * (0.5 + 0.5 * grain));\\n    }\"}], \"TargetFile\":\"/src/three/island/textures.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Refining height AO cavity curve\", \"toolSummary\":\"Refine height-to-AO mapping\"}"
