  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Evaluating Home Page Updates**\n\nI\'m now integrating `<HostingCategories />` into `/src/pages/Home.tsx`. I\'m also checking quick link placements in `PlansHighlight.tsx`. I\'m evaluating two options: directly including `/bots` alongside `/plans` and `/vps`, or relying solely on `<HostingCategories />` for those links. I need to see which approach creates the most intuitive and clean design for the user.\n\n\n**Designing Bot Hosting Pages**\n\nI\'ve moved on to designing `/src/pages/BotHosting.tsx`. The aim is a clean, honest presentation. I\'m focusing on a dedicated header, including an eyebrow and heading, along with a concise description emphasizing Miami, USA infrastructure and straightforward CTAs. A crucial \"Owner Confirmation\" banner will explain proposed pricing and resource limits, including supported runtimes. Plus, I will include a Miami Infrastructure Card. Five distinct bot hosting tiers are planned: Pollen, Dewdrop, Nectar, Petal, and Blossom.\n\n\n**Constructing Tier Comparisons**\n\nI\'m now building the detailed comparison tables for the five bot hosting tiers. This includes dedicated grids for resource allocation (RAM, vCPU, NVMe storage), location, use cases, and prices. I\'m carefully integrating a \"Draft\" status with disabled CTAs to prevent premature checkout. I\'m also preparing a comparison of confirmed versus proposed features, including automated node setups. I\'ll also add a comparison of hosting options.\n\n\n**Implementing VPS Hosting**\n\nI\'m now implementing the FAQs accordion using the necessary components. Furthermore, I\'m working on `/src/pages/VpsHosting.tsx` (Phase 5). I\'ve added a header with confirmed CTAs and all five KVM VPS plan cards with dynamic CTA button text, which check for the availability of direct product URLs. The CTA navigates to the billing store for pending URLs and adjusts to direct deployment when available. I\'ve also incorporated a full VPS comparison table for all five tiers, which will facilitate a direct order process.\n\n\n**Expanding Hosting Comparisons**\n\nI\'m now expanding the comparison of available regions and platform infrastructure, including Singapore, Miami, and India, detailing AMD Ryzen, Intel Xeon Gold, DDR5, NVMe, and Cloudflare integration, plus DDoS protection. I\'m also adding recommended workload cards, as well as an improved comparison between Minecraft, VPS, and Bot Hosting via `<HostingComparison />`. I\'ve also incorporated a VPS FAQs accordion.\n\n\n\n"
