    captured_user_requests {
      text: "# PETALNODES \342\200\224 COMPLETE WEBSITE DEVELOPMENT & BRAND UPDATE (MASTER PROMPT)\n\nYou are continuing development of the existing Petalnodes website.\n\nYour responsibility is to complete the remaining website development, update all hosting categories, implement the new Cherry Blossom plan naming system, create missing pages, improve visual quality, and ensure the entire website feels like one polished, professionally designed hosting platform.\n\n**IMPORTANT: Do not rebuild the website from scratch.** Inspect the existing repository, documentation, components, routes, content modules, assets, and current implementation first. Preserve everything that already works. Improve and extend the existing project rather than replacing it unnecessarily.\n\nAll website content must be written in professional, natural English.\n\n---\n\n# 1. BRAND INFORMATION & IMPORTANT URLS\n\nBrand: Petalnodes\n\nMain Website:\nhttps://petalnodes.cloud\n\nBilling / Store:\nhttps://billing.petalnodes.cloud\n\nClient Area:\nhttps://billing.petalnodes.cloud\n\nGame Panel:\nhttps://panel.petalnodes.cloud\n\nDiscord:\nhttps://discord.gg/GS3wuc4HGk\n\nStatus Page:\nhttps://status.petalnodes.cloud\n\nUse these exact URLs wherever applicable.\n\nSocial media:\n\n- YouTube: Petalnodes\n- X (Twitter): @petalnodes\n- Instagram: @petalnodes\n- TikTok: Not available. Do not display it.\n\nVerify actual social profile URLs before linking them. If a profile URL cannot be verified, leave it as TODO.\n\n---\n\n# 2. CHERRY BLOSSOM PLAN NAMING SYSTEM\n\nThis is a critical branding update.\n\nRemove the old generic names such as Dirt, Stone, Lapis, Diamond, Netherite, Warden, Dragon, Starter, Basic, Pro, Advanced, and Ultimate from active hosting plan displays.\n\nUse the following exact new names.\n\n## A. Minecraft Hosting \342\200\224 7 Plans\n\n| Plan | RAM | CPU | NVMe Storage | Price |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Seed | 2GB | 100% | 10GB | \342\202\27159/mo |\n| Sprout | 4GB | 150% | 15GB | \342\202\27199/mo |\n| Sapling | 8GB | 250% | 25GB | \342\202\271169/mo |\n| Blossom | 12GB | 350% | 35GB | \342\202\271239/mo |\n| Grove | 16GB | 400% | 45GB | \342\202\271299/mo |\n| Orchard | 20GB | 500% | 55GB | \342\202\271369/mo |\n| Sakura | 24GB | 600% | 65GB | \342\202\271449/mo |\n\nUse these exact names, specifications, and prices.\n\nKeep the existing plan purchase links attached to their corresponding plans if they are already configured and verified. Never accidentally transfer one plan\'s checkout URL to another plan.\n\nIf a checkout URL is missing, leave it as TODO and ask me for it.\n\n### Minecraft Hosting Specifications\n\n- Java & Bedrock Support\n- Paper\n- Purpur\n- Fabric\n- 2 Allocations\n- 2 Database Access Slots\n- NVMe Storage\n- DDoS Protection\n- Daily Backups Included\n\nDo not claim Forge, NeoForge, or other software support unless verified.\n\n## B. VPS Hosting \342\200\224 5 Plans\n\nUse these exact names:\n\n| Plan | RAM | vCPU | NVMe Storage | Price |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Root | 4GB | 2 | 20GB | \342\202\271300/mo |\n| Branch | 6GB | 2 | 30GB | \342\202\271500/mo |\n| Trunk | 8GB | 3 | 40GB | \342\202\271800/mo |\n| Canopy | 12GB | 4 | 60GB | \342\202\2711,200/mo |\n| Evergrove | 16GB | 4 | 80GB | \342\202\2711,600/mo |\n\n### VPS Specifications\n\n- KVM Virtualization\n- Full Root Access\n- Linux OS\n- IPv4 Subject to Availability\n- Network Protection\n- Discord Support\n- NVMe Storage\n- Daily Backups Included\n\n### Infrastructure\n\nOur infrastructure includes:\n\n- AMD Ryzen processors\n- Intel Xeon Gold processors\n- DDR5 memory\n- NVMe storage\n- Cloudflare protection\n- DDoS protection\n\nDo not claim every VPS uses the same processor or that every location has identical hardware.\n\nDo not invent CPU generations, clock speeds, network speeds, bandwidth limits, or DDoS mitigation capacity.\n\nKeep existing verified billing links attached to the correct plans. Ask me for missing links.\n\n## C. Free Minecraft Server Rewards\n\nRename the free server tiers as follows:\n\n| New Name | Invites Required | RAM |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Petal I | 6 | 2GB |\n| Petal II | 8 | 5GB |\n| Petal III | 12 | 7GB |\n| Petal IV | 16 | 9GB |\n| Petal V | 20 | 13GB |\n| Petal VI | 30 | 17GB |\n\n### Rules\n\n- Member Leave: \342\210\2222\n- Rejoin: \342\210\2221\n- Fake / Alt Account: \342\210\2222\n- Mass Ping: Invite Reset\n\nClaim through a Discord Support Ticket.\n\nKeep all requirements and rules unchanged.\n\n## D. Discord Boost Rewards\n\nRename the boost tiers:\n\n| New Name | Active Boosts Required | RAM |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| Bloom I | 1 Boost | 3GB |\n| Bloom II | 2 Boosts | 6GB |\n| Bloom III | 3 Boosts | 9GB |\n| Bloom IV | 4 Boosts | 12GB |\n\n### Specifications\n\n- Java & Bedrock\n- NVMe Storage\n- Claim through a Discord Support Ticket\n- Active boosts are required to maintain rewards.\n\nMake the active boost requirement clearly visible.\n\nDiscord:\nhttps://discord.gg/GS3wuc4HGk\n\n## E. Bot Hosting\n\nAdd Bot Hosting as a completely separate hosting category.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Dedicated Bot Hosting page.\n- Attractive introduction and feature section.\n- Plan comparison layout.\n- Resource specifications.\n- Supported bot environments and languages.\n- Purchase or enquiry CTA.\n- Discord support link.\n- Billing link where appropriate.\n\nBot Hosting plan names, prices, RAM, CPU, storage, and supported runtimes have not yet been provided.\n\nDo not invent them.\n\nUse the same botanical naming philosophy as the rest of Petalnodes. Suggest suitable names and ask me before finalizing them.\n\n---\n\n# 3. WEBSITE PAGES TO CREATE\n\nCreate fully designed, functional pages for:\n\n1. Documentation / Knowledge Base\n2. Terms of Service\n3. Privacy Policy\n4. Service Level Agreement\n5. Server Locations\n6. Contact\n7. About\n8. Modpacks\n9. VPS Hosting\n10. Bot Hosting\n\nDo not create empty placeholder pages.\n\nEvery page must use the existing Petalnodes design system, typography, textures, animations, navigation, footer, and responsive layouts.\n\n## Documentation\n\nCreate an organized knowledge base with categories:\n\n- Getting Started\n- Minecraft Server Setup\n- Java & Bedrock\n- Server Software\n- Plugins and Mods\n- File Management\n- Backups\n- Server Configuration\n- Troubleshooting\n- Billing and Account Help\n\nOnly document features that actually exist or are confirmed.\n\n## Legal Pages\n\nCreate professionally structured initial drafts for:\n\n- Terms of Service\n- Privacy Policy\n- SLA\n\nDo not invent legally binding policies, refund guarantees, uptime guarantees, data-retention periods, compensation commitments, jurisdiction, or business registration details.\n\nClearly mark unconfirmed information for owner review.\n\nAsk me for missing legal details one question at a time.\n\n## Server Locations\n\nOur available locations:\n\n- Singapore (SG)\n- Miami (USA)\n- India (IN)\n\nCreate an attractive location page using a map, location cards, or another suitable visual presentation.\n\nWe also have VPS infrastructure.\n\nDo not invent datacenter addresses, latency figures, network capacity, or location-specific hardware availability.\n\n## Contact Page\n\nInclude:\n\n- Discord support.\n- Billing link.\n- Client area.\n- Relevant contact information only when confirmed.\n\nDo not invent email addresses or phone numbers.\n\n## Modpacks Page\n\nCreate a properly designed Modpacks page explaining available modpack support and how customers can use it.\n\nOnly display modpacks that are actually available or verified.\n\n---\n\n# 4. HARDWARE, SECURITY & TRUST CONTENT\n\nUse the following confirmed information:\n\n- NVMe storage.\n- Daily backups included.\n- AMD Ryzen processors.\n- Intel Xeon Gold processors.\n- DDR5 memory.\n- Cloudflare protection.\n- DDoS protection.\n- Singapore, Miami, and India locations.\n\nUpdate the existing hardware, security, and trust sections.\n\nDo not invent:\n\n- Exact CPU model numbers.\n- Exact network speeds.\n- Backup retention periods.\n- Uptime percentages.\n- DDoS mitigation capacity.\n- Guaranteed support response times.\n\nYou may display:\n\n- \"Daily Backups Included\"\n- \"NVMe Storage\"\n- \"DDR5 Memory\"\n- \"DDoS Protection\"\n- \"Cloudflare Protection\"\n\nDo not add unsupported numerical guarantees.\n\n---\n\n# 5. COMPLETE THE EXISTING WEBSITE\n\nInspect the original project documentation and all existing implementation before making changes.\n\nThe existing website already has a substantial implementation, including:\n\n- Home page with a six-chapter 3D scroll story.\n- Seed \342\206\222 Roots \342\206\222 Shield \342\206\222 Instant Build \342\206\222 Neighbors \342\206\222 Bloom storytelling.\n- Procedural voxel textures.\n- Custom ink-sketch reveal shader.\n- Story navigation.\n- Static fallback.\n- Reduced-motion support.\n- Minecraft hosting plans.\n- Comparison table.\n- FAQ.\n- Trust sections.\n- Footer.\n- 404 page.\n- Development galleries.\n\nThese features must be audited, not blindly rebuilt.\n\nCheck all original build requirements and identify:\n\n- COMPLETED\n- NEEDS IMPROVEMENT\n- NOT IMPLEMENTED\n\nComplete the missing requirements without damaging working features.\n\nPay special attention to:\n\n- Scroll restoration.\n- Reverse scrolling.\n- Story navigation.\n- Context loss handling.\n- Mobile rendering.\n- Static fallback.\n- Reduced motion.\n- Responsive pricing tables.\n- Accessibility.\n- SEO.\n- Performance.\n\nDo not assume previous test results prove the current repository is still correct. Run the actual checks again.\n\n---\n\n# 6. TEXTURE QUALITY \342\200\224 MAJOR IMPROVEMENT\n\nThe existing procedural textures must be reviewed and significantly improved.\n\nI want genuinely high-quality, realistic voxel block textures.\n\nThe current problem is that basic procedural textures can look flat, artificial, repetitive, or low quality.\n\nImprove the materials so they look like carefully crafted physical voxel blocks.\n\nInspect and improve:\n\n- Cherry leaves.\n- Cherry logs.\n- Cherry planks.\n- Grass.\n- Dirt.\n- Stone.\n- Deep stone.\n- Glow ore.\n- Paths.\n- Paper lanterns.\n- Moss carpets.\n- All other existing block materials.\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Detailed surface variation.\n- Natural color variation.\n- Convincing depth.\n- Realistic roughness.\n- Proper height maps.\n- Normal maps derived from the same height information.\n- Natural edge wear.\n- Surface imperfections.\n- Carefully balanced texture contrast.\n- Consistent lighting response.\n- No obvious repeated patterns.\n- No flat, plastic-looking surfaces.\n\nPreserve deterministic procedural generation and the existing 64\303\22764 texture requirement unless the original implementation explicitly supports a compatible higher-resolution approach.\n\nMaintain nearest-neighbour pixel treatment where required by the art direction.\n\nNever sample, trace, or copy vanilla Minecraft textures or Mojang assets.\n\nImprove the texture development gallery so materials can be inspected properly, including their faces, normal maps, and material appearance.\n\nKeep performance and mobile compatibility in mind.\n\nDo not sacrifice the existing static fallback.\n\n---\n\n# 7. EXISTING VISUAL DESIGN\n\nPreserve the original Petalnodes Cherry Blossom art direction.\n\nThe website should feel like a beautifully crafted sketchbook-inspired voxel world.\n\nMaintain:\n\n- Paper and ink visual language.\n- Cherry blossom environment.\n- Hand-drawn details.\n- Realistic voxel blocks.\n- Shader-lit scenes.\n- Natural lighting.\n- Soft shadows.\n- Paper grain.\n- Sketch effects.\n- Existing 3D storytelling.\n- Existing animations.\n- Responsive layouts.\n- Static and reduced-motion fallbacks.\n\nAvoid:\n\n- Generic purple, indigo, or violet gradients.\n- Glassmorphism.\n- Frosted-glass cards.\n- Generic SaaS hosting templates.\n- Stock photos.\n- Unsplash images.\n- Emoji-based feature icons.\n- Generic three-icon feature grids.\n- Neon effects on dark UI.\n- Unrelated visual themes.\n\nKeep the existing Mojang disclaimer exactly:\n\n\"Not an official Minecraft product. Not approved by or associated with Mojang or Microsoft.\"\n\n---\n\n# 8. NAVIGATION & FOOTER\n\nOrganize the navigation clearly:\n\n- Home\n- Minecraft Hosting\n- VPS Hosting\n- Bot Hosting\n- Server Locations\n- Documentation\n- Discord\n- Client Area\n\nFooter links:\n\n- Billing\n- Client Area\n- Game Panel\n- Status\n- Documentation\n- Terms of Service\n- Privacy Policy\n- SLA\n- Contact\n- About\n- Modpacks\n- YouTube\n- X\n- Instagram\n- Discord\n\nHide links whose destinations are not verified.\n\nDo not display TikTok.\n\nKeep the footer consistent with the existing design.\n\n---\n\n# 9. CENTRALIZED CONTENT MANAGEMENT\n\nUse the existing central content/configuration module for all important website information.\n\nCentralize:\n\n- URLs.\n- Social links.\n- Minecraft plans.\n- VPS plans.\n- Bot Hosting plans.\n- Free server rewards.\n- Boost rewards.\n- Prices.\n- Resources.\n- Specifications.\n- Locations.\n- FAQs.\n- Legal content.\n- Navigation.\n- CTA labels.\n\nDo not scatter important business information across unrelated components.\n\nEnsure that plan names, resources, prices, and checkout URLs remain correctly associated.\n\nRemove outdated names from active website content.\n\nDo not remove historical documentation or internal migration references unnecessarily.\n\n---\n\n# 10. REACT BUTTON COMPONENT INTEGRATION\n\nInspect the previously provided React button component source completely.\n\nExtract its useful functionality and adapt it to the existing Petalnodes design system.\n\nPreserve useful interactions:\n\n- Hover animations.\n- Press interactions.\n- Touch feedback.\n- Accessible focus states.\n- Keyboard interaction.\n- Button variants.\n- Disabled states.\n- Loading states.\n\nDo not blindly integrate every visual effect.\n\nExclude:\n\n- Glassmorphism.\n- Liquid glass effects.\n- Metallic gradients.\n- Visual styling that conflicts with the Petalnodes sketchbook aesthetic.\n\nInstall only genuinely required dependencies.\n\nDo not introduce unnecessary libraries.\n\nDo not replace every existing button automatically. Inspect and integrate carefully.\n\n---\n\n# 11. ASK ME ABOUT MISSING INFORMATION \342\200\224 ONE QUESTION AT A TIME\n\nYou must interact with me to collect missing business information.\n\nAsk exactly ONE clear question at a time.\n\nWait for my answer before asking the next question.\n\nDo not ask questions whose answers are already provided in this prompt.\n\nPrioritize these missing details:\n\n1. Minecraft plan-specific checkout URLs.\n2. VPS plan-specific checkout URLs.\n3. Bot Hosting plan names and resources.\n4. Bot Hosting prices and supported runtimes.\n5. Backup retention period.\n6. Exact network speed, if confirmed.\n7. Support response-time expectations.\n8. Refund policy.\n9. Uptime commitment and SLA terms.\n10. Legal business details.\n11. Verified social profile URLs.\n12. Any other important information needed to publish accurate content.\n\nIf I do not know an answer, let me skip it.\n\nKeep skipped details as TODO.\n\nDo not invent answers.\n\n**Important:** Do not stop all development while waiting for information. Complete everything that can safely be implemented without the missing details.\n\nFor legal or policy content, distinguish clearly between a draft and an approved policy.\n\n---\n\n# 12. FINAL IMPLEMENTATION & QUALITY CHECKS\n\nAfter implementation:\n\n- Verify every route.\n- Verify every navigation link.\n- Verify all external URLs.\n- Verify every hosting plan name.\n- Verify every plan\'s RAM, CPU, storage, and price.\n- Verify checkout links are attached to the correct plans.\n- Verify free server reward requirements.\n- Verify boost reward requirements.\n- Verify desktop layouts.\n- Verify mobile layouts.\n- Verify static mode.\n- Verify reduced-motion behavior.\n- Verify the existing 3D story.\n- Verify all new pages.\n- Verify all CTAs.\n- Check accessibility.\n- Check SEO metadata.\n- Check structured data.\n- Check for broken images and missing assets.\n- Check for outdated plan names.\n- Run tests.\n- Run type checking.\n- Run the production build.\n- Run the existing release checks.\n\nDo not remove or weaken tests to make the project pass.\n\nDo not mark a task complete unless it has actually been implemented and verified.\n\n---\n\n# 13. FINAL REPORT\n\nWhen the work is complete, provide:\n\n1. All pages created.\n2. Existing pages updated.\n3. Minecraft Hosting final plans.\n4. VPS Hosting final plans.\n5. Free Server reward tiers.\n6. Discord Boost reward tiers.\n7. Bot Hosting implementation status.\n8. Texture improvements.\n9. Button component integration.\n10. All remaining TODOs.\n11. Decisions requiring my approval.\n12. Test results.\n13. Typecheck results.\n14. Production build results.\n15. Remaining bugs or limitations.\n\n---\n\n# EXECUTION ORDER\n\nFollow this order:\n\n**Phase 1 \342\200\224 Project Audit**\nInspect the existing repository, documentation, current implementation, and remaining TODOs.\n\n**Phase 2 \342\200\224 Centralized Data Update**\nUpdate all confirmed business information, URLs, hosting plans, rewards, and new Cherry Blossom names.\n\n**Phase 3 \342\200\224 Missing Pages**\nCreate Documentation, Legal, Locations, Contact, About, Modpacks, VPS, and Bot Hosting pages.\n\n**Phase 4 \342\200\224 Texture Improvements**\nImprove procedural materials and texture previews without breaking the existing 3D world.\n\n**Phase 5 \342\200\224 Existing Website Completion**\nComplete missing original build requirements and improve responsive behavior, accessibility, SEO, and performance.\n\n**Phase 6 \342\200\224 Button Integration**\nAdapt the supplied React button component to the existing design.\n\n**Phase 7 \342\200\224 Verification**\nRun the full test, typecheck, build, and release checks.\n\n**Phase 8 \342\200\224 Owner Questions**\nAsk me one question at a time for the remaining business information. Continue independent implementation while waiting for answers.\n\nStart by inspecting the existing project. Do not immediately rewrite components or rebuild pages.\n\nThe final result must be a cohesive, premium Petalnodes hosting website with a consistent Cherry Blossom identity, accurate business information, polished interactions, and genuinely high-quality visual details."
    }
