      text: "# PETALNODES \342\200\224 FINAL TODO ELIMINATION, BOT HOSTING LAUNCH & VPS OPTIMIZATION\n\nContinue working on the existing Petalnodes website and repository.\n\nA significant amount of development has already been completed. Do not repeat completed work or rebuild the website.\n\nYour primary objective is to identify every remaining TODO, complete all work that can be completed safely, create a complete Bot Hosting product category with proposed plans, and thoroughly finalize the existing VPS Hosting experience.\n\nIMPORTANT: Inspect the actual current repository before making changes. The completion summary below describes previously reported work, but you must verify the current code rather than assuming everything is still correct.\n\n# PHASE 1 \342\200\224 COMPLETE PROJECT AUDIT\n\nInspect the entire project, including:\n\n- All source files.\n- All routes and pages.\n- Central content/configuration modules.\n- All TODO and FIXME comments.\n- DevTodoBadge components.\n- Release-check scripts.\n- Missing URLs.\n- Unfinished sections.\n- Unimplemented features.\n- Draft legal pages.\n- Incomplete documentation.\n- Missing metadata.\n- Broken links.\n- Incomplete CTAs.\n- Unfinished mobile layouts.\n- Any unfinished visual or functional details.\n\nRun:\n\n`npm run check:release`\n\nInspect the actual implementation of every reported TODO.\n\nThe previous reported release check contained 57 TODOs:\n\n**18 blocking URL TODOs:**\n- 7 Minecraft Paymenter checkout URLs.\n- 5 VPS Paymenter checkout URLs.\n- 3 Bot Hosting URLs.\n- 3 social profile URLs.\n\n**39 draft-detail TODOs:**\n- Bot Hosting specifications and runtimes.\n- Support email and hours.\n- Backup retention.\n- Provisioning rules.\n- Upgrade rules.\n- Refund rules.\n- Geyser port guide.\n- Legal entity details.\n- Jurisdiction.\n- SLA targets.\n- Other unconfirmed business information.\n\nThese numbers are from the previous report. Run the current release check and use its actual output as the source of truth.\n\nCreate a complete categorized report:\n\n1. COMPLETED\n2. PARTIALLY COMPLETED\n3. NOT IMPLEMENTED\n4. BLOCKED BY MISSING OWNER INFORMATION\n5. ACTUAL BUGS\n6. EXTERNAL ENVIRONMENT ISSUES\n\nDo not classify a task as blocked if you can complete it without owner information.\n\n# PHASE 2 \342\200\224 FIX ALL REMAINING IMPLEMENTATION WORK\n\nWork through every TODO that can be completed independently.\n\nExamples:\n\n- Finish incomplete documentation.\n- Improve unfinished pages.\n- Complete responsive layouts.\n- Fix broken internal navigation.\n- Fix broken CTA destinations.\n- Improve missing SEO information.\n- Complete accessibility improvements.\n- Remove outdated plan references.\n- Fix incomplete comparison tables.\n- Improve error states and empty states.\n- Complete missing page metadata.\n- Improve the footer and navigation.\n- Finish incomplete FAQs.\n- Complete existing feature descriptions.\n- Fix actual application bugs.\n- Improve loading and fallback states.\n- Remove unnecessary duplicate components.\n- Clean up unused code when safe.\n\nDo not simply hide TODO indicators to make the release check pass.\n\nDo not remove TODO tracking unless the underlying work is actually complete.\n\nDo not invent business facts to satisfy release checks.\n\nFor information that requires my confirmation, preserve a clearly tracked owner TODO.\n\nContinue implementing independent work even when some URLs or policies are unavailable.\n\n# PHASE 3 \342\200\224 BOT HOSTING: CREATE A COMPLETE PRODUCT CATEGORY\n\nBot Hosting must become a proper Petalnodes hosting product.\n\nCreate a polished dedicated page at:\n\n`/bots`\n\nAlso integrate Bot Hosting into:\n\n- Homepage hosting categories.\n- Main navigation.\n- Footer.\n- Hosting comparison sections where appropriate.\n- Relevant FAQs.\n- SEO metadata.\n- Central content module.\n\n## Infrastructure\n\nOur Bot Hosting servers will run on VPS infrastructure located in Miami, USA.\n\nUse the Miami location for the Bot Hosting infrastructure.\n\nDo not accidentally describe Bot Hosting as running on Singapore or India infrastructure.\n\n## Create the Bot Hosting Plan System Yourself\n\nI want you to design a complete botanical-themed Bot Hosting plan lineup.\n\nDo not leave the Bot Hosting page with only three empty draft cards.\n\nCreate a sensible progression of plans with:\n\n- Attractive botanical plan names.\n- RAM allocations.\n- CPU allocations or fair-use limits.\n- NVMe storage.\n- Monthly pricing proposals in INR.\n- Suitable bot hosting use cases.\n- Plan comparison.\n- Feature inclusions.\n- Upgrade progression.\n\nUse a consistent naming style that fits Petalnodes and its Cherry Blossom identity.\n\nYou may use names inspired by:\n\n- Pollen\n- Dewdrop\n- Nectar\n- Petal\n- Blossom\n- Sakura\n\nChoose the best names and create a coherent plan hierarchy.\n\n### Resource Planning\n\nDesign resource allocations that are practical for common workloads such as:\n\n- Discord bots.\n- Telegram bots.\n- Node.js applications.\n- Python applications.\n- Small automation services.\n- Lightweight always-on applications.\n\nDo not promise unlimited CPU, unlimited resources, or unrestricted usage.\n\nClearly distinguish guaranteed RAM from shared CPU allocations and fair-use limits.\n\n### Pricing\n\nCreate sensible proposed monthly prices in INR.\n\nUse the existing Petalnodes Minecraft and VPS pricing as reference points.\n\nDo not copy VPS pricing directly for shared bot hosting.\n\nKeep all proposed Bot Hosting plans marked as DRAFT / OWNER APPROVAL REQUIRED until I approve the pricing and actual resource capacity.\n\nDo not create fake Paymenter product links.\n\nDo not activate checkout buttons for plans that do not yet have real checkout URLs.\n\n### Bot Hosting Features\n\nDesign the page around relevant features, but distinguish between implemented capabilities and proposed features.\n\nPotential features to investigate and include only when actually supported:\n\n- 24/7 bot hosting.\n- Node.js support.\n- Python support.\n- Application startup and restart.\n- Console access.\n- File management.\n- Environment variables.\n- Dependency installation.\n- Logs.\n- Automatic restart after crashes.\n- Resource monitoring.\n- Backups.\n- Easy deployment.\n\nInspect the actual panel and infrastructure capabilities before claiming these features are available.\n\n# PHASE 4 \342\200\224 MIAMI LOCATION & 2MS PING CLAIM\n\nBot Hosting will use Miami VPS infrastructure.\n\nThe desired latency claim is approximately 2ms.\n\nHowever, do not publish a universal 2ms guarantee without evidence.\n\nInvestigate:\n\n- Where the Miami VPS is physically hosted.\n- Whether the 2ms figure has an actual measurement source.\n- Which network probe or client location produced the measurement.\n- Whether it is a local datacenter measurement or an end-user measurement.\n- Whether latency is stable and repeatable.\n\nIf 2ms is verified only from a specific measurement location, state that limitation clearly.\n\nIf it is not verified, do not advertise it as a guaranteed customer ping.\n\nUse honest wording such as:\n\n\"Miami-based infrastructure\"\n\nIf supported by verified testing, you may use a qualified claim such as:\n\n\"Approximately 2ms latency from the tested network location.\"\n\nNever claim that every customer worldwide will receive 2ms ping.\n\nDo not fabricate ping tests, traceroutes, benchmark screenshots, or latency statistics.\n\n# PHASE 5 \342\200\224 VPS HOSTING FINALIZATION\n\nThe VPS page already exists at:\n\n`/vps`\n\nReview and improve it rather than rebuilding it.\n\nOur confirmed VPS plans are:\n\n| Plan | RAM | vCPU | NVMe Storage | Price |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| Root | 4GB | 2 | 20GB | \342\202\271300/mo |\n| Branch | 6GB | 2 | 30GB | \342\202\271500/mo |\n| Trunk | 8GB | 3 | 40GB | \342\202\271800/mo |\n| Canopy | 12GB | 4 | 60GB | \342\202\2711,200/mo |\n| Evergrove | 16GB | 4 | 80GB | \342\202\2711,600/mo |\n\nConfirmed specifications:\n\n- KVM Virtualization.\n- Full Root Access.\n- Linux OS.\n- IPv4 Subject to Availability.\n- Network Protection.\n- Discord Support.\n- NVMe Storage.\n- Daily Backups Included.\n\nInfrastructure includes:\n\n- AMD Ryzen processors.\n- Intel Xeon Gold processors.\n- DDR5 memory.\n- NVMe storage.\n- Cloudflare protection.\n- DDoS protection.\n\nImprove:\n\n- VPS plan cards.\n- Comparison table.\n- Technical specifications.\n- Location information.\n- Use-case explanations.\n- Purchase CTAs.\n- Mobile responsiveness.\n- SEO.\n- FAQs.\n- Visual consistency.\n\nClearly explain the difference between Minecraft Hosting, VPS Hosting, and Bot Hosting.\n\nDo not invent hardware generations, CPU clock speeds, bandwidth, network speeds, uptime, or guaranteed performance.\n\nKeep the Cherry Blossom plan names exactly as provided.\n\n# PHASE 6 \342\200\224 COMPLETE DOCUMENTATION\n\nReview `/docs`.\n\nComplete the documentation structure and write useful, practical guides.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n1. Getting Started.\n2. Creating a Minecraft Server.\n3. Java and Bedrock Connection.\n4. Paper, Purpur and Fabric.\n5. Installing Plugins.\n6. File Management.\n7. Server Backups.\n8. Server Configuration.\n9. Troubleshooting.\n10. Billing and Account Access.\n11. VPS Getting Started.\n12. Bot Hosting Getting Started.\n\nFor the Bot Hosting and VPS guides, document only capabilities that have been verified.\n\nDo not create fake panel instructions or unsupported feature tutorials.\n\n# PHASE 7 \342\200\224 LEGAL & POLICY TODOs\n\nReview:\n\n- `/terms`\n- `/privacy`\n- `/sla`\n\nThese pages currently contain draft content.\n\nImprove their formatting, clarity, navigation, and organization.\n\nHowever, do not invent:\n\n- Legal business identity.\n- Registered address.\n- Jurisdiction.\n- Refund policy.\n- Cancellation conditions.\n- Backup retention.\n- Uptime commitment.\n- SLA compensation.\n- Guaranteed support response time.\n\nKeep unconfirmed clauses clearly marked for owner approval.\n\nDo not represent draft policies as approved legal documents.\n\n# PHASE 8 \342\200\224 VERIFY THE EXISTING TEXTURE WORK\n\nThe procedural texture system has already received substantial improvements.\n\nPreviously reported improvements include:\n\n- 14 procedural 64\303\22764 block materials.\n- Worley cellular patterns.\n- Domain-warped FBM.\n- Sobel normal maps.\n- Roughness maps.\n- Corrected DataTexture.flipY orientation.\n- Deterministic generation.\n- Quality tiers.\n- Instance tinting.\n- Daylight, Sunset and Lantern previews.\n\nDo not redo this work unnecessarily.\n\nInspect the current implementation and only fix remaining visual or technical issues.\n\nPreserve performance, mobile compatibility, and the existing sketchbook aesthetic.\n\n# PHASE 9 \342\200\224 CHECK THE PREVIOUSLY REPORTED BROWSER ERRORS\n\nA previous report identified errors originating from a Chrome extension attempting to overwrite `window.fetch` in a browser context where it was read-only.\n\nDo not modify application code to work around an unrelated browser extension unless the actual Petalnodes application is independently affected.\n\nVerify in a clean browser session.\n\nReport separately:\n\n- Actual Petalnodes application errors.\n- Browser extension errors.\n- Build errors.\n- Test errors.\n\nNever claim an application bug is fixed merely because an extension was disabled.\n\n# PHASE 10 \342\200\224 CENTRALIZED CONTENT & CONSISTENCY\n\nKeep all important business information in the existing central content module.\n\nCentralize:\n\n- URLs.\n- Social profiles.\n- Minecraft plans.\n- VPS plans.\n- Bot Hosting plans.\n- Rewards.\n- Specifications.\n- Locations.\n- FAQs.\n- Policies.\n- Support information.\n- CTA labels.\n\nEnsure plan names, prices, resources, and URLs are never mismatched.\n\nRemove outdated active plan names from visible website content.\n\nDo not scatter business information across components.\n\n# PHASE 11 \342\200\224 OWNER QUESTIONS\n\nAsk me exactly one question at a time for details that genuinely require my approval.\n\nPrioritize:\n\n1. Missing Minecraft checkout URLs.\n2. Missing VPS checkout URLs.\n3. Bot Hosting pricing and resource approval.\n4. Bot Hosting checkout URLs.\n5. Verified social profile URLs.\n6. Support email and hours.\n7. Backup retention.\n8. Refund and cancellation policy.\n9. Uptime and SLA targets.\n10. Legal business information.\n11. Verification of the 2ms latency claim.\n\nDo not ask me about details that are already confirmed.\n\nIf I answer \"skip\", keep that item as TODO.\n\nDo not stop the implementation process while waiting for answers.\n\n# PHASE 12 \342\200\224 FINAL VERIFICATION\n\nRun the actual project checks:\n\n- Unit tests.\n- SSR tests.\n- TypeScript.\n- Lint.\n- Production build.\n- Release checks.\n- Browser verification.\n\nVerify:\n\n- Homepage.\n- Minecraft plans.\n- VPS.\n- Bot Hosting.\n- Locations.\n- Documentation.\n- Modpacks.\n- About.\n- Contact.\n- Terms.\n- Privacy.\n- SLA.\n- 404.\n- Static fallback.\n- Reduced-motion mode.\n- Mobile layouts.\n- Desktop layouts.\n- Navigation.\n- Footer.\n- External URLs.\n- Purchase buttons.\n- All plan resources and prices.\n\nCheck for:\n\n- Broken links.\n- Missing images.\n- Console errors.\n- Horizontal overflow.\n- Incorrect plan names.\n- Mismatched checkout URLs.\n- Unsupported claims.\n- Incomplete pages.\n\nDo not remove or weaken tests to achieve a passing result.\n\n# PHASE 13 \342\200\224 FINAL REPORT\n\nProvide a detailed report showing:\n\n1. All remaining TODOs discovered.\n2. TODOs completed.\n3. TODOs still blocked by missing owner information.\n4. Actual bugs fixed.\n5. VPS improvements.\n6. Bot Hosting plans created.\n7. Proposed Bot Hosting prices and resources.\n8. Miami infrastructure verification.\n9. Whether the 2ms claim was verified.\n10. Documentation completed.\n11. Legal pages status.\n12. Test results.\n13. Typecheck results.\n14. Production build results.\n15. Remaining issues.\n\n## EXECUTION INSTRUCTION\n\nStart by auditing the actual repository and running the release check.\n\nThen complete all independent unfinished work.\n\nCreate the full Bot Hosting plan lineup as proposed drafts, improve VPS Hosting, and finish all remaining pages and features.\n\nAsk me for owner-only information one question at a time.\n\nDo not rebuild working features, do not invent business claims, and do not hide unfinished work.\n\nThe goal is to bring Petalnodes as close as possible to a complete, production-ready hosting website with a consistent premium Cherry Blossom identity."
    }
  }
}
